  ('zcrm_1579374000043500003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447288', 'Michael Sherman', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request, I will cancel ASi, Sedera &amp; FTNI.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-11-18 07:45:01', '2019-11-18 07:45:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043467013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021903046', 'Paul Pepin', NULL, '1-15-19 Brenda called me back and likes the PDHC with Redirect at $1000/$350 and we''ll cancel MPB Select membership bc Paul is aging out and can''t keep membership. Brenda successfully cancelled membership and asked to have $100 or $125 fee waived. She wrote in the notes per my request.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-15 16:50:32', '2019-11-15 17:16:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043467008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021903046', 'Paul Pepin', NULL, '11-15-19 Patti asked me to call this client. I just left them a vm and told them I will help with the change in their membership to walk them through the process.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-15 16:37:00', '2019-11-15 16:37:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043467003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044733004', 'Elizabeth Ball', NULL, '11-15-19  62, healthy, no meds, no pre-x, no tobacco. LHS member now but didn''t realize their struggles. Was told Sedera was more affordable. Looking at DPC called Balanced Health who does not promote health ins or health sharing or anything. Asked if I know of another one in Greeley and found Nextera there as well. Balanced Health is $119 and Nextera $99. So, she will look at Nextera too!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-11-15 16:28:23', '2019-11-15 16:28:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043433084', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027993160', 'Karen Peirson', NULL, 'Karen called to get the best price and place to get a nuclear thyroid scan- I told her that she would need to get a hold of Sedera for that and gave her their number.  She then asked, due to the fact that she has been a member with us for 4 years, if her thyroid condition was now shareable.  I then told her that her start date was Jan 2019, and she said "oh, I thought it was longer.  So I''m not even into year 2 yet am I?"  I told her unfortunately no. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-11-15 15:59:28', '2019-11-15 15:59:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043433079', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013233147', 'Karl E. Schoepflin', NULL, 'Karl called in again needing some hand holding when it came to having some lab work done, how he would go about it.  I told him that it would be the same instructions I gave before, no different, to use the script I had given him.  I asked if he checked to make sure that the bloodwork was coded as preventative, and he hadn''t - so my only suggestion was going to be to ask either the doctor''s office or the lab if it is.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-11-15 14:46:16', '2019-11-15 14:46:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043433074', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919976', 'Randal Warwick', NULL, 'same as note below....I created a ticket for it because he called in again. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-11-15 14:38:43', '2019-11-15 14:38:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043433069', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000035547456', 'Joan Tekula', NULL, 'Called Joan back and her questions were the fact that her doctor is trying to set her visit up as a 2 or 3 part deal where she comes in for an "initial visit" before the actual routine visit and then come back again to do the blood work. She said absolutely no way is she going to do it that way because the provider is just trying to get money out of her. Me and Patti told her that no, only the routine screening visit is what is covered. Everything has to be done as 1 visit and it has to be preventative ONLY. So she asked if after her blood work is done and the doctor calls her to let her know everything is ok or if there is some issue that it is her choice weather she wants to go back in or not but it would NOT be covered if she choose to go in. That would be considered Diagnostic and she would be paying out of pocket. She 1 million percent understood and said that''s all she needed to hear. She defiantly understands about the providers trying to get more money with different visits and she also totally understands about the whole making sure they Code everything as Preventative, if not then it will not be covered and she will need to get back with the provider and have them re code everything and re submit the bills. She gets it. Everything was answered that she needed to be. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-11-15 13:54:47', '2019-11-15 13:54:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043446153', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043460179', 'Jason Steinberg', NULL, 'Acct set up charged 11/15. Billing set up to start 11/22. Good to go for 12/1', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-11-15 13:52:13', '2019-11-15 13:52:13'),
