Sent by MPowering Benefits Broker on 11/14/2019.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-11-14 11:36:48', '2019-11-14 11:36:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000043385003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041185005', 'James Roberts', NULL, 'James called me and wanted to make sure he was doing the right thing for needing to go to his local orthopedist for trouble he has been having with his hip. He said he did the teladoc and they told him anti inflammatory and  trying to keep off of it for a couple days. He said he did everything they said and it did not fix his issue and pain. So now he wants to take it to a specialist and will most likely be getting and MRI and imaging done. I told him that anything with that is considered Injury/Illness and Diagnostic in nature. When it comes to that he will presenting himself as a cash pay patient at any facility of his choosing, there is no network he needs to stay in and it can be any provider of his choice. I let him know that he ONLY pays out of pocket up to his $500 IUA. Anything after that is when Sedera steps in. I explained who Sedera is and what they do, he 100% knew everything I was talking about and just wanted to make sure he was correct. He absolutely was and I told him it is always best to call into me first before doing anything just to make sure, He seemed very knowledgeable with everything that involves his plan. He said he took a LOT of notes during his Welcome Call. I told him that was a very good idea because sometimes all the different portions of the plan can get a little confusing going back and forth and trying to remember all the different names and vendors of his plan, but he seemed to have everything down pat. Very MPowered Member :) Lastly I told him it is probably wise to call Sedera now ahead of time to just let them know what is going on and that he is most likely going to be needing their help. I told him that they would be more than happy to help guide you along the process so you are doing everything correctly, which he has done so far. James was happy and generous that I took the time to sit down and explain everything to him over the phone. I told him to be on the lookout for an email I will be sending that will be explaining how he will be submitting his bill''s over to Sedera so they have the proof that you paid up to his IUA. So in regards to that I told him to keep every single receipt  and bill that he pays for proof to Sedera that you met your IUA. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-11-14 11:04:10', '2019-11-14 11:04:10'),
