  ('zcrm_1579374000043333003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016068140', 'Michele Venne', NULL, 'Michele emailed me back about this billing issue she is having in regards to a mammogram she went and had. It was Breast Tomosynthesis BI. This type of mammogram is not something is covered. the only way it can be covered is if it was written out by her provider for having dense breasts. She stated that is exactly why she had the type of mammogram done because the last time she had a mammogram the provider requested for her to have a second mammogram done and an MRI for having dense breast''s. So I asked her to send me the Detailed Medical Bill with the CPT Codes on it to be able to determine what specific procedures were done and why are you are being billed. The only thing she got back was something that the provider "texted" her apparently. I told her what she was given was just a statement and had no codes on there that would help us. So again I asked for her to get the bill with the CPT Codes on it. This morning she emailed me back with this: Hi Kelly-

I called the company, and was given these two CPT codes: 77063   77067

I no longer have the printout from the doctor''s office about which mammogram she requested, but I can probably get another copy. I''m thinking she requested that particular kind because I told her the last time I had one done, I had to go back for a second mammogram and an ultrasound (all came back fine) because of dense breasts. 

Let me know what else I need to do.
Thanks
Michele

I told her that this will NOT work. We can NOT take codes that are just written down. We need have the the actual physical bill with those codes on them. I responded to her saying all this and am waiting for a response. I can tell she is not going to be happy with all this back and forth and just wants this solved. There is nothing we can do about that. I let her know there is nothing that we can do without that bill with codes. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-11-13 12:47:09', '2019-11-13 12:47:09'),
