  ('zcrm_1579374000042776021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007792019', 'Carolyn Hope Clark', NULL, '10-31-19 I guess I will stay put for another year. My Drs are all still covered with Anthem and I am comfortable with my current premiums.

It looks like I don’t need to do anything to renew if I stay with my current plan is that correct? I updated all my info this summer when I moved. 

Thanks Wendy!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-31 17:10:44', '2019-10-31 17:10:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042776016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041406092', 'Pratik Patil', NULL, 'Pratik called with a few questions and really just an understanding of what to expect as a new member.  I sent him a Welcome call scheduler but told him to schedule either the 2nd or the 3rd week so that he had everything in front of him as we go over how his plan works with him.  Also I emailed Jennifer at RCI to ask that the misspelling on the RCI card would be fixed and resent. Also going to email Sunny because Pratik was trying to get back into his portal to check on his billing. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-31 16:56:49', '2019-10-31 16:56:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042776011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043013154', 'Jani Osborne', NULL, '12-31-19 Shannon''s friend. Healthy, no pre-x, has masters in nutrition, yogi, etc. Paying $530 now! She''s 48. Does her annual physical every other year. She''s interested in the SDHC and PSDHC but her docs are not in the PHCS network, so I recommended SDHC. She will weigh differences. She''s leaving country Nov. 14th so we are talking Tuesday of next week. Email ACA compliant wellness items.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-31 16:46:24', '2019-10-31 16:46:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042776006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007168187', 'Lili Walker', NULL, 'she called in very distraught over the fact that she has a$31,000 medical bill that Liberty just isn''t paying she cannot find any help when calling them and wanted our help.  After I spoke with Patti to confirm that Lili was indeed cancelled (and owed $700 in unpaid bills)  I let Lili know that she was cancelled last year and that she no longer has any service through us.  She tried to argue that she has service through the 20th of Nov, and I told her that it was not true.  I told her that sadly it was.  She begged for help and advice - I told her to just hound Liberty daily- knock on their door until you get a response. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-31 15:18:10', '2019-10-31 15:18:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042693217', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042738276', 'Joshua Latham', NULL, 'Member &amp; Ch $2500 IUA 40-49 SD', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-31 13:51:14', '2019-10-31 13:51:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042747023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000045841172', 'Shoshana Kressler', NULL, '10-31-19 They are now a family of 4 revisiting this as an option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-31 13:48:50', '2019-10-31 13:48:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042747018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013233147', 'Karl E. Schoepflin', NULL, 'Called into get "the word from the horses mouth" he appreciated everything that his wife was doing for him but he just wanted to hear it from us and ask a number of questions.  So I went over the entire plan basically- answered his questions went over all the templates I would be sending- he wanted them sent to his email specifically. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-31 13:33:06', '2019-10-31 13:33:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042693212', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529553', 'Shelly Jamieson', NULL, 'Shelly called in and asked more questions about husbands torn ACL.  They got recommendation for surgery that will cost $20k.  Provider called Sedera for "preapproval".  I told her that that was not how this worked and that this was not "insurance". I asked if she had paid anything out of pocket she said that the just got 1st office visit bill for app $460. I advised her of her $1500 IUA and that she would have to pay that.   She told me that she had opened a need and that the 2nd MD was in process.  But they wanted to schedule the surgery.  I told her that this was a process and that didn''t happen intermediately.  Advised that all further contact needed to be with Sedera as we do not have any access to the records  due to privacy laws.  Thanked me for my answers.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-31 13:26:10', '2019-10-31 13:26:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042717038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011716025', 'Richard O''Krepki', NULL, 'Richard called in and said that 2 different providers needed"Permission" to speak to whoever they need to to verify his benefits. I told him that is not me and that it would be whomever his MEC is. I pulled up his profile and while it was loading I asked what he was needing to be done(he said the word procedure)? He said that he has a Lypoma which is a fatty deposit. I then let him know that he would actually be contacting Sedera. This type of situation he would be paying out of pocket up to his $1500 IUA. This is an injury/illness and ANYTHING along those lines is not covered and he would present himself as a cash pay patient. But ONLY up to the $1500. Once he is close to that or he knows that the bill is going to be more than that he contacts Sedera ASAP. I explained in full what Sedera does and how all of the diagnostic portion of his plan works. He understood and going to see if he can get a price point and work it out from them. I advised him to contact Sedera regardless so they know what is going on. It is a type of surgery. Even though it is something small there are always many different fees that are involved. Something that is 100 bucks could turn out to be 800. He got it and took down their number and will call them when he is does getting a price worked out. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-31 13:25:08', '2019-10-31 13:25:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042747013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044826001', 'Tracy Hritz', NULL, '10-31-19 Tracy is 55 and her kids are 21 and 24 independent, so not included. Tracy did have a melanoma removed from her wrist. So, told her to check her records to make sure she knows what to expect if something comes back. She will also find out the cash pay price for PCP Aspen Medical. Came highly recommended via Alicia who is dealing with her own health issues and tested the membership already. Tracy is paying $960 for 2020 and more in 2019 around $1200! She reviewed Sedera''s site, Karis Group, 2ndMD....  She was reviewing BBB reviews, etc. Likes the $1500/$335 or $1000/$350.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-31 12:52:45', '2019-10-31 12:52:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042693207', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919520', 'Dechen Hawk', NULL, 'I determined that we were reimbursed by Sedera for his Tobacco Surcharge for the months of July &amp; August 2019. (September previously refunded)  I will send check out to him via US mail today.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-31 12:50:47', '2019-10-31 12:50:47'),
