  ('zcrm_1579374000042622040', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000044406197', 'Suzanne Muller', NULL, '10-28-19 Suzanne has gone w/o ins for 1 1/2 years as self-employed person couldn''t afford $400+ / $7K ded. Healthy, no meds, no tobacco. Did have melanoma removed in Aug. of this year and paid cash of about $650 which about 30% discount she thought. She wants to continue to use Planned Parenthood for wellness and buy Self Directed Healthcare to be able to afford the monthly cost and be prepared for catastrophe if something happens.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-28 17:40:53', '2019-10-28 17:40:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042622035', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000061006173', 'Brian Delaney', NULL, '10-28-19 Brian had 4 surgeries recently for shoulder and knee. Still has some chronic shoulder issues to be concerned about. Otherwise, healthy and 50 years old paying $550-$600 month. Interested in Provider Directed with Redirect bc price difference is so small. They want to ponder information and decide what''s best. They also want to talk with Dwight''s and Roger''s.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-28 16:24:50', '2019-10-28 16:24:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042622024', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000002630141', 'Cameron Elmendorf', NULL, '10-28-19 Cameron Elmendorf and Brian Delaney are now divorced but looking into this together for family, knowing they have to join separately.  Cameron goes to her annual pap every year and dermatologist 2x year. Daughter had 1x dr. visit this year but usually never except wellness.  They are interested in PDHC with Redirect bc price difference is so negligible. Paying $800 for her and daughter with Anthem BCBS now.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-28 16:19:08', '2019-10-28 16:20:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042622016', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042696196', 'Daniel McManus', NULL, 'Danny is enrolling now. $1500/$290 Redirect. Complete and all set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-28 14:06:14', '2019-10-28 14:19:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614182', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042610147', 'Sarah Marshall', NULL, 'Billing set up for 11/1 start.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 13:41:54', '2019-10-28 13:41:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042622008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011447107', 'Emily Takahashi', NULL, '10-28-19 Emily is comparing this to trad ins via another broker. She is earning too much for a subsidy. So, this is a no brainer. She''s 60 now and talked about $1500/$507 PDHC with Redirect as best option. She likes what she hears and will let me know after she talks with other broker.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-28 13:28:58', '2019-10-28 13:29:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614177', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042610147', 'Sarah Marshall', NULL, 'Member only $500 IUA 40-49 SD', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 12:49:48', '2019-10-28 12:49:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614172', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000035227061', 'Marie Folsom', NULL, 'Marie called in and asked why the pharmacy was not accepting her "insurance card" for her prescriptions. I let her know that there is no coverage with prescriptions and that she absolutely does NOT show her card for that. She was very confused by this. I explained in FULL how it works and what we do for prescriptions. I told her that the only thing that we do when it comes to that is she either can call in with the name, dosage, and quantity or she can fill out a form with all that info on it. What I would do then once I got all that info is, look the medication up on a couple websites that I use and get decently priced coupons for whatever medication she was prescribed. I would send it either through an email attached OR I can have the coupon texted to her phone number that she gives me. She was perfectly fine after I explained all of that to her. She sounded a lot more relieved that there was at least SOMETHING we can do for her prescriptions. When I told here there is not anything that get "Covered" by her card or anything like that, she was really upset. But since there is the coupon''s that I can find her she was LOT more relieved. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-28 12:48:05', '2019-10-28 12:48:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614167', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042610147', 'Sarah Marshall', NULL, 'Per John this member started her app on 10/19 and had issues.  Didn''t finish until 10/25 will enroll her and set up in FTNI.  John to send file to Sedera.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 12:45:46', '2019-10-28 12:45:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614162', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610208', 'Marc Krawatsky', NULL, 'Hillary called in and just needed to know about the pre authorization for her getting a Mammogram. She gave me the place she has been going to for the last few years while being with us and ASI. She just wanted to double check and make sure they are still in network and they are. She also gave me the name of her OBGYN whom she has been going to as well and the are in network too. So she is all set with those 2 appointments she needs to make. She lastly needed me to look up a provider in her area  for her Wellness Visit to have her annual physical. I looked up some providers and sent her the list via email. I also let her know I would be sending a couple other emails just to refresh her on how she presents herself with her MEC Card and I also sent an email that has 5 steps that can use to avoid surprise billing. I made it clear to her to make sure she lets the provider know everything is to be strictly Preventative and coded as preventative CPT Codes. She FULLY understood and is all set with her yearly appointments she needs to make. She was very happy that I took the time to explain everything and all the emails that I am sending her to help as well so she does not need to sit there and try and remember everything I had just said. She is VERY VERY good about being Preventative and making sure everything is done correctly. She has not has one billing issue with her providers or anything along those lines since she has been a member. Hillary thanked me up and down and will be sure to read all the emails I sent her in full. She really wants to make sure she does everything correctly. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-28 12:34:05', '2019-10-28 12:34:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614157', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041829001', 'Kruti Patel', NULL, 'Paper app emailed to ASi as this member enrolled through Selerix.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 12:13:22', '2019-10-28 12:13:22'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614152', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041829001', 'Kruti Patel', NULL, 'Employee Only $500 IUA ASi MEC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 12:12:29', '2019-10-28 12:12:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614147', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000052185004', 'Brian Keith', NULL, 'Member called in and was unclear as to what he would pay every month.  Both Kelly and I explained that he would not pay his IUA every month, only when incurring a need.  finally got that across to him.  Also told me his wife uses Natropathic providers, I explained to him that whole area, lack of CPT codes, treatment plan submission  &amp; mostly Out of pocket.  He will talk this over with his wife.  I told him that he would have to speak w/Ron again prior to enrolling.  Verified email &amp; contact #', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 10:52:01', '2019-10-28 10:52:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614070', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015735109', 'Steve Moeller', NULL, 'Steve just called in and said that when he went for his dermatology appointment he got sent a bill saying he needed to pay.  Steve stated that he thought this type of appointment was covered 100%. I let him know that unfortunately that kind of appointment is considered injury/illness and is not preventative. He seemed a little bummed when I told him this. So I explained how it works with Sedera and his IUA. He completely understood and said the bill was only about $700 and his IUA is $1500, so he will just pay it. I let him know to make sure that he keeps his receipts for anything that he paying out of pocket because he will need to submit those over to Sedera when the time comes for them to jump in and help out after he reached his IUA. He was fine with all of this and thanked me very much for explaining everything to him and will pay the bill and save everything. I let him know that I will send an email to him that explains how to submit his bills to Sedera and also told him their phone number and information is in the email for when he calls them. The last thing I sent him was the Sedera Access Guidelines that are up to date. I let him know that going through the guidelines would be a good idea to help him know what is shared and what not. He had asked what is shared and what is considered Preventative. That email will help him and his wife out a lot. He was very thankful for all the information and always is very very nice whenever I speak with him. He is very easy going and has never gotten upset or anything along those lines. He is always just looking to figure everything out and wants to stay on top of everything. I would say he is a very Empowered member!! :) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-28 08:52:50', '2019-10-28 08:52:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042309116', 'James Maynard', NULL, '2nd request sent for submission of Proof of DPC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 08:27:34', '2019-10-28 08:42:08'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042614008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041664048', 'Akihito Ishiwatari', NULL, 'Sent 2nd request for Submission of Proof of DPC', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-28 08:24:30', '2019-10-28 08:24:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042616027', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042221122', 'Sarah Wright', NULL, 'As suspected November came back with the same message. Sent second email and let her know we cannot start her if a payment is not received by 11/1', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-10-28 07:56:49', '2019-10-28 07:56:49'),
