Chelsey Williams 
</chelseyraejean@gmail.com>', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-10-24 11:55:47', '2019-10-24 11:55:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042560003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000043030038', 'Kathleen Naman', NULL, '10-24-19 Kathy is 63 turning 64 in March of 2020. She''s a self-employed psychotherapist in Boulder. She''s a Cloud Medical client and Loves them! She''s also a LHS member and sees all of the horrible reviews out there and wants to move asap. Earliest start date is Dec. 1 which is also her renewal date with LHS. We have an enrollment date for next week, same time. She''s on synvastatin 10 mg for high cholesterol and is well managed for many years. Also depression meds flouxitine which is also well managed and see can seek help when needed since she''s in the biz. Cloud costs her $119 a month and $1500 IUA DPC is $402 mo to equal $521.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-24 11:51:45', '2019-10-24 11:51:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042551003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624180', 'Samantha Pasley', NULL, 'Samantha called in and told me that her daughter had had food poisoning while they were on vacation and that she had paid her $1000 IUA and uploaded all her bills to Sedera.  She was now at quest and they were going to do further testing for her stomach.  Asked was this connected to original need.  I advised that it would be connected to original need.  Asked should she pay out of pocket, I told her to contact Sedera and ask her needs counselor.  She will contact.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-24 09:56:47', '2019-10-24 09:56:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042537003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000040874041', 'Robert McCord', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Requested RCI cards also for their two son''s that are in other states. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-10-24 08:04:28', '2019-10-24 08:04:28'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042507013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028115309', 'Jennifer Rulon', NULL, 'Jeni called in to get a refresher on her plan and how everything works, we talked awhile and I answered and explained things for her.  I told her that I would be sending a bunch of educational emails her way. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-23 16:05:27', '2019-10-23 16:05:27'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042510003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005568233', 'Sherry Lewis', NULL, 'Kelly Cheever requested for myself to contact client and re-educate the client on proper  preventative care procedures and about using in-network PHCS practitioners thru the ASI network.  Attempted to call client at number on account.  Was unable to leave a message because voicemail was full....will attempt at a later date.  Will encourage Kelly Cheever to send her an email with my phone number to set up an appropriate time to further re-educate client on proper use of the preventative network through ASI...will continue to follow up.', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2019-10-23 15:31:54', '2019-10-23 15:31:54'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042507008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021903103', 'Jodi Anglin', NULL, 'called to be reminded of how to get to her HRA to update some info- I guided her to the site and gave username and password.  all set. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-23 15:23:11', '2019-10-23 15:23:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042506008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042508013', 'Susan Fecko', NULL, '10-23-19 Susan is interested in MCS but she has MS. It''s supposedly 10 years in remission but she''s nervous about the symptom portion of the pre-x clause. I agree! It''s not worth the risk with her condition. Her boyfriend is part of One Share Health in Basalt. That''s a new one! Susan does a lot of alternative medicine like acupuncture, etc. She''s 50 and lives in Boulder. SHe''s paying $550 with Cobra and it''s ending at the end of the month. She will really need to explore traditional options instead. She already has a broker so I didn''t go down that path with her.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-23 14:45:15', '2019-10-23 14:45:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042507003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005568233', 'Sherry Lewis', NULL, 'Sherry called to ask if a flu shot was considered a covered service, I told her that it is, if the doctor is in network.  She told me that she was at the doctor- she said that she ended up going to see the nurse practitioner that I told her wasn''t in network.  She said that she ended up going to her anyway....because she wasn''t going to see the doctor for a wellness check anyway....but that it was going to be out of pocket.  So she asks if she could have the front desk split her bills to show that one of the in network doctors administered the flu shot so that it would be covered.  I took a long pause and told her that she could try doing it, but that it was making the situation extremely convoluted and that I could not make any promises on whether or not she would be held responsible for paying this/these bills.  Not the answer she wanted, but she told me she was going to ask that it be so.  I had spent so much time on digging into checking and seeing if this doctor was in network or not because she told me that this was a wellness visit, then finding other doctors that were in the same practice that WERE in network.  I went over every single email that I sent to her on preventive care, she even started the conversation with "Hi Kelly, it''s me Sherry, you sent me all of the emails?" She complained that the staff she spoke with told her that they never found a nomination for her doctor (she filled it out less than a week ago) then she complained that staff told her that the list I gave her was old and that one of the doctors on the list left the practice 10 years ago.  I told her that although that was unfortunate, I got the name/names off of the multiplan site,  MPowering Benefits has no control over it.  She said asked me if the mammogram would be billed separately- placing it in network, I told her no, not if it is linked to that doctor.  I went over all of this before her appointment today and she chose to act and then ask later.  -KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-23 14:40:10', '2019-10-23 14:40:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042506003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037141445', 'MarySue Bonetti', NULL, '1-23-19 Just left her a vm to help her with any outstanding challenges. Told her I''m sorry to hear of the horrible news. UGH!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-23 14:29:39', '2019-10-23 14:29:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042505003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000003496005', 'Matthew Stull', NULL, 'A ticket was made at 8:51 AM this morning for a couple questions about paying for a couple different procedures he is needing to have done to him next week in regards to his heart. See Ticket. That''s all updated there in the tickets for Mr. Stull. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-23 14:26:24', '2019-10-23 14:26:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042503003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012535076', 'Todd Lary', NULL, 'Todd called our office today and wanted to speak to me because he turned 65 on Sept. 9th.  Discussed with Patti and Rod, Rod wants him off Asi asap.  I instructed him to send in the termination letter for his current plan.  We discussed Diane and their 2 kids who still need coverage.  I took him to my click funnel and we discussed Diane''s options.  They do use a DPC so we talked about that plan.  They currently have the PSD plan (old Sedera Select).  He decided they want to remain on the PSD (Access) plan.  Enrollment fee is $25.  He will discuss with Diane and I told him to send the cancellation letter asap and be sure to enroll before 11-20 for a 12-01 effective.  Patti also said they will be covered on the old plan up to Dec. 1st since they have already been billed which I shared with Todd.', 'Ron Patterson', 'Ron Patterson', '2019-10-23 14:17:02', '2019-10-23 14:17:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042487008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041271091', 'Roy Simmons', NULL, 'Called member to respond to question about HRA.  I let him know that his cards were mailed out to him on 10/11 and that is what he should use to do the HRA.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-23 12:57:09', '2019-10-23 12:57:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042487003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039419008', 'Dean Sawyer', NULL, 'I called Christine and left her a VM  in response to her call about MPB cards.  I let her know cards were sent out to her on 8/30 and let her know what address we had for he.  Directed her to call me if it was different.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-23 12:52:26', '2019-10-23 12:52:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042477003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529553', 'Shelly Jamieson', NULL, 'Shelly emailed me concerning her husband having a torn ACL and not knowing how to pay for the whole surgery that is scheduled to be soon.  I sent her my advice- to call Sedera and go through 2nd MD.  I sent instructions on how to open up a need. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-23 11:50:03', '2019-10-23 11:51:02'),
