  ('zcrm_1579374000042335018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011919617', 'Heather Davies', NULL, 'Heather called in today and needed some help with finding providers in her area. She needed help with a gynecologist, gastroenterologist, and to double check if her primary care was still in network. Her primary care is still in the network and I found 2 lists for her for the other 2 types of providers. I sent her the list and explained to her what she needs to do for preventative care and how she presents herself. I also sent her a few emails that will help explain things to her better. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-21 14:04:04', '2019-10-21 14:04:04'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042351013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025370156', 'Jennifer Bianchi', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request I will cancel RCI, Sedera &amp; cancel pmt in FTNI.  Member never had welcome call', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-21 13:05:49', '2019-10-21 13:10:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042335013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017078004', 'Jason Scheier', NULL, 'Jason called and asked what he needs to do when it comes to his doctor recommending him to see a specialist. He has a stye on his eye that is not going away and he now needs to go see an eye doctor. I explained to him how that works with him having to pay out of pocket for situations like this. I let him know what his IUA is and how he goes about paying for that. I told him who Sedera is and when they come into play and what they do. I told him this would be considered his first "Need". He totally understood everything I told him and I recommended that he call Sedera to let them know ahead of time. I gave him Sedera''s phone number and he will be calling them to give them a heads up and ask any other questions he might have about this. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-21 12:52:16', '2019-10-21 12:52:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042351008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001165323', 'Kevin Schill', NULL, 'Member called in and let us know that app 18 mos ago he was billed $2000 for a preventative visit &amp; blood work.  Provider agreed to take $300 network price and bill was paid.  He was balance billed and was told that he was in collections.  I directed him to Leena @ ASi to get this straightened out.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-21 12:06:49', '2019-10-21 12:06:49'),
