  ('zcrm_1579374000042189018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033574112', 'Brianne Spitz', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request I will cancel RCI &amp; Sedera &amp; pmt in FTNi', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-17 12:29:30', '2019-10-17 12:29:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042189013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041185005', 'James Roberts', NULL, 'What I received back was this members RCI card.  So I will resend to him.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-17 12:26:14', '2019-10-17 12:26:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042180013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624180', 'Samantha Pasley', NULL, 'Sherry from Advanced Radiology called in and needed to speak to someone about reviewing Samantha''s benefits. I asked what was going on and she said she had her yearly checkup for a mammogram and they found abnormalities and that is the appointment Samantha is at now, for diagnostic. I told Sherry when it comes to ANYTHING that is diagnostic and non preventative there are no "Benefits". The member pays out of pocket up until their IUA amount, in Samantha''s case is $1000. Anything after that she is going to need to get in contact with Sedera ASAP. I told Sherry Sedera is the portion of her plan that helps with the rest of the billing after the IUA is met and proven that it was met for anything Diagnostic. That is all that she is going to do is pay out of pocket and I told Sherry to tell Samantha to keep the receipt for proof of payment to Sedera when the time comes. Sherry told me the bill is about $250, so she does not need to contact Sedera just yet. All she is doing today at the appointment is paying the amount of the bill since it is nowhere near her IUA of the $1000. Sherry thanked me for taking the time to speak with her and explain everything Samantha is good to go! -K', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-17 12:21:23', '2019-10-17 12:21:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042180008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041152005', 'Krista Barker', NULL, 'Wanted to know how getting the Flu shot works as in what and how does she go get it done while being covered. I told her if she or her kids provider does them during annual wellness visits then you can most certainly get it done during the exam and that is 100% preventative, it would not cost extra or anything along those lines. She said her kids'' provider does that so she is good to go with her kids. For her I told her she can get it done at any local pharamcy and pay for it out of pocket and then she keeps the receipt and send it into RCI and they will reimburse her for it. Was very happy to hear how easy that was!! Thanked me very much and said it was awesome she got to speak to a real person and not some robot. I told her nope, there will never not be a live person. Even for the messages you leave if no one answers. It is an answering service but with real people and they send the message out to whomever it needs to go to! She was THRILLED about that. Very happy NEW Member. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-17 12:12:01', '2019-10-17 12:12:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042189008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041185005', 'James Roberts', NULL, 'Per Vanessa during Welcome call member update his address.  Previous day I received his fulfillment pkg back.  I will update w/RCI &amp; Sedera &amp; FTNI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-17 12:01:55', '2019-10-17 12:01:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042190008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025283259', 'Julie Oldham', NULL, '10-17-19 Choosing to keep her PSDHC to keep tax benefits with HSA and $96 write off with ins component.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-17 11:51:46', '2019-10-17 11:51:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042190003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042338001', 'Nancy Lattin', NULL, '10-17-19 Has a chip on her should but appreciated my information. She''s 59 and turning 60 in June 2020. She''s currently part of Dr. Jennifer Lentz''s DPC and really likes her! She was part of another one that didn''t provide as comprehensive memberships. She works in the medical records industry since 18 and highly knowledgeable about how that works. She has scoliosis since teen but hasn''t been treated for it since then but may need PT or imotrin from time to time. No meds, healthy otherwise. Currently members of LHS and used them for mammogram which cost $2200 and she paid her IUA of $500 for it and the rest was reimbursed. Dr. Lentz can get it for $99 which is what she will do this year. She is opposed to brokers getting paid monthly for assisting her. She wants to get away from that entirely. She is highly opposed to her cost increasing from $245 month with $1000 IUA DPC at 59 to $425/$1000 once her renewal and she''s 60. Wants the cost to be determined by her health status. Not going to pay that much more since she''s healthy. She moved back to CO from MA where the costs was apparently much more affordable. She doesn''t like that she can''t go direct to Sedera an Individual either and wants smaller groups to be allowed since she has contract workers. Full of complaints but wants to sit on it and for me to send her the information to read. I didn''t go into problems with LHS since she had a fine experience last year.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-17 11:38:47', '2019-10-17 11:38:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000042175038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041357028', 'Juan Andrade', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online the 30 minute welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-10-17 11:38:44', '2019-10-17 11:38:44'),
