  ('zcrm_1579374000041921013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010331105', 'Kathleen White', NULL, 'Kathleen''s doctor found that she was anemic and might need to do an iron infusion based on a follow up blood test this evening- I went over the needs process and sent Kathleen the appropriate email. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-11 16:46:02', '2019-10-11 16:46:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041887066', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031391042', 'Jonathan VanNoy', NULL, 'Left message for Nicole Vannoy ...waiting on call back...', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2019-10-11 16:09:57', '2019-10-11 16:09:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041915036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171479', 'John Raker', NULL, '10-11-19 Curious about other memberships. Suggested Redirect since only $3 more a month at the $500 IUA / $378 month. He''s paying $375 now for PSDHC. He will lose HSA compliance which he''s fully funding now. But, interested in HMA as well. Sending him info on REdirect.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-11 15:45:42', '2019-10-11 15:45:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041915031', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000060480020', 'Marian Salley', NULL, '10-11-19 Marian is an EMDR therapist. She''s 51 and paying $900+ mo for trad insurance. She has lymphoma which is currently in remission for the last 1 1/2 years. Says she''s had it for last 20 years and treatment is needed on and off. She understands completely about the pre-x clause. I explained it to her in every way possible. I''m also asking her to read the cancer section and pre-x section when she received the Guidelines to make sure she has no confusion at all.  She sees an oncologist 2x per year for preventative check up and she knows those costs will be her responsibility to pay for. She also takes compounded HRT and pays for that on her own now bc ins. doesn''t cover it. She will keep paying with this. She is healthy otherwise and does not use tobacco. She would be a good candidate for the HMA perhaps in a separate conversation. She mountain bikes and such to keep in shape. Recommending Redirect since she''s 51.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-11 15:33:49', '2019-10-11 15:33:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041921008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027283187', 'Joan Wood', NULL, 'wanted help in finding a clinic for a flu shot.  I told her that I would help her find something in network.  I sent the list to her as well as a multiplan link. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-11 15:20:16', '2019-10-11 15:20:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041921003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171479', 'John Raker', NULL, 'John called in for guidance of how his MEC card and benefits work.  I spoke with him at length and went over everything.  He asked me if there were any new plans that have come out since he has joined.  He mentioned seeing the DPC one- so I touched on that and Redirect as well, I told him that the VPC is new to us but that Wendy could help explain it better than I .  He wanted to know the costs of these other plans.  I told him that Wendy would be able to help with that.  I told him that I would reach out to Wendy and ask her to contact him.  He was very grateful for all of the help. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-11 14:56:10', '2019-10-11 14:56:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041887061', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010340031', 'Kevin Delaney', NULL, 'Kevin called in and had a a lot questions. He first wanted to know how to "check on himself in the system" and where his "link" is to send to people to refer them and show them what he is doing. I stopped him and said I am sorry but that is not how it works. You can always call into here and I will help guide him to where he needs to go or answer the questions myself if I am able to. I explained how his entire plan works and what the difference is between Preventative and Diagnostic care. I told him when he needs to make an appointment he will call into me here and I will look up what type of provider he needs and send him the list via email. I told him that is what his first step is going to me. Calling in here and making sure there are providers in the network for him. Once we have found a list he will then choose which provider and call and make an appointment. I told him that he needs to make sure the appointment is Preventative ONLY and to stress this to the provider, and also that the bills HAVE to be coded as preventative and not as diagnostic. Otherwise it will not be covered. I told him when it comes to an emergency or  anything that is Injury/Illness than he pays out of pocket up to his IUA of $500. I told him that once he is close to his IUA he needs to contact Sedera. I explains who Sedera is and how all of that process works to submitting his bills to them. I made it very clear that he needs to have a Welcome Call, because he has not had one yet and has been enrolled for 2 years now. I told him that it is very very important and the welcome call will cut out a lot of questions that he might have. I told him I will be emailing him the Welcome Call Scheduler and to book an appointment for that ASAP. There are several other emails that I will be sending him as well. The 64+ Preventative Services that are mandated and sharable by the ACA, submitting bill to Sedera, welcome call booker, wellness instructions for how he will be presenting himself at his preventative appointments, and 5 steps to avoid surprise bills. Kevin was very confused on how everything works and I am hoping this has helped him out. He seemed to understand everything a lot better after talking to him and he is going to book a welcome call asap. I let him know that the Welcome Call is only about 15-20 minutes long and to make sure he has that amount of time to spare when making the appointment. -KF', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-11 14:41:14', '2019-10-11 14:49:49'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041915018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041953021', 'Barbara Batt', NULL, '10-11-19 Barb 55 is healthy, no pre-x, no tobacco, rarely goes to Dr. She lives in CO now but is planning to live in RV and travel around the country soon. She''s paying $600+ to Bright Health now with $7900 Ded or MOP. Redirect is $335/$1500 for her and will work well while she travels around the country. Katie Marshall referred her but Katie and Penny Ridley never became members. Completed enrollment in 1st call. Very pleased.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-11 13:37:57', '2019-10-11 14:20:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041887056', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026335249', 'Terrie Parrott', NULL, 'Member submitted Member Change form to change address I will change in all vendors', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-11 13:14:57', '2019-10-11 13:14:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041915008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015979073', 'Tomi Hanson', NULL, '10-11-19 Tomi Hanson reached out to Ameritas directly to cancel his dental and vision plan as of October 1st. Can you please verify and cancel as of 9/30/19 and refund any premiums collected for October for the below policies.
               Spirit Dental – 995638131

               Direct Vision – 997018154
Please let me know when complete so I can inform the client.

Thank you,

Teresa Stein | Agent Concierge 
Direct 651.419.6255', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-11 13:10:19', '2019-10-11 13:10:19'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041915003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000000165438', 'Gladys Diaz-Jourdain', NULL, '10-11-19 Called to ask about filing taxes. Sent her instructions and called her back. She said she figured it out already. All set!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-11 13:07:32', '2019-10-11 13:07:32'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041887051', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028522022', 'Matthew DePofi', NULL, 'Member called in and had some questions about his plan.  I noticed that he had not had his Welcome call as yet and told him that that is very important and would answer all of his questions.  He then asked me about how this would be handled in an ER situation.  I told him that unless he was in a life threading situation avoid the ER at all costs.  Use Urgent Care.  Explained about IUA and the saving of bills and how a need works.  He wanted to know if Ambulance or Lifeflight would be shareable as he hikes alot and sometimes he does this remotely.  I told him that it would be if medically necessary.  I also sent him the Welcome call scheduler.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-11 12:52:12', '2019-10-11 12:52:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041900008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041271091', 'Roy Simmons', NULL, 'Called in for his RCI card.  Requested Patti to order new cards and send a pdf', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2019-10-11 12:46:37', '2019-10-11 12:46:37'),
