  ('zcrm_1579374000041587026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036209064', 'Damian Smith', NULL, 'Jacci called in to speak with someone in finance.  I told her that Sunny would reach out to her tomorrow.  I sent the payment update form. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-02 16:49:21', '2019-10-02 16:49:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041610013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014431007', 'Suzanne Cote', NULL, '10-2-19 Called to inquire about how to handle what to do when abroad. I explained she must pay the fee and if/when the cost exceeds her IUA then she can submit for reimbursement. But, she must pay them directly. She understands.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-02 16:30:15', '2019-10-02 16:30:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041587021', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017078069', 'Lauren Ankenman', NULL, 'Lauren called to get record of financial info for when she was enrolled with us.  I told her that I would pass the request onto Sunny, she asked for Sunny''s email instead and I gave it to her. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-10-02 15:54:20', '2019-10-02 15:54:20'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041610008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041616103', 'Kai Philipp Olshausen', NULL, '10-2-19 Enrollment complete for SDHC family of 4. He''s getting kids SS#''s and will call Patti directly by tomorrow.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-02 14:36:53', '2019-10-02 14:36:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041594043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011881700', 'Thomas (Tom) Traxler', NULL, 'Member called into update his CC.  I will send him the Payment update form.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-02 13:44:25', '2019-10-02 13:44:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041607018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610380', 'Laura Watson', NULL, 'Laura called in and said she needs some help with submitting a need to Sedera and the process. I told her about her IUA and she stated she most certainly has paid up to the $1500, I then started to say I was going to send an email that explains how to submit the bills to them and she cut me off and said that she has done that already. So she then continues to interrupt me and said that she is also waiting to hear back from someone about the 2nd MD process she has done. She said the surgery is for her son and that the doctor gave her a negotiated price of a cash pay discount and that she needs to pay in FULL 2 days before the surgery or the doctor will NOT do the surgery. I told her that if she has already been in contact with Sedera and started the "Needs" process then that is who she needs to contact, not me. She told me that Darius told her that the next step and to get things moved along faster is to call me here "MPowering Front Desk Concierge" is who she needs to contact. I apologized and told her that Idk why he would tell her this, I started to say what my position is because she asked and when I said that we on our end here at MPowering do not have any of the info on file or anything when it comes to Sedera and she hung up on me. This is the 4th time that Darius has told his members that their next step is to call me and I will be able to speed things along and give them any information they need. THIS IS NOT TRUE!!!! Now Laura is extremely upset because she is being told the wrong information and that she wasted her time with calling me and most likely is going to cancel after her son''s surgery. Very Very Very unhappy member and me as well. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-02 13:19:42', '2019-10-02 13:19:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041577025', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599111', 'Matthew Vendetti', NULL, 'Acct Set Up charged, billing set to start 10/22. Good to go for 11/1 start', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-10-02 12:52:13', '2019-10-02 12:52:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041577020', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599062', 'Alexander Allison', NULL, 'Acct set up fee charged, billing set to start 10/22. Good to go for 11/1', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-10-02 12:47:21', '2019-10-02 12:47:21'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041607013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027885127', 'Bergen Kunselman', NULL, 'Bergen called because she needed to know what her IUA was to be able to open and HSA. She said whomever it was that she would be dealing with opening an HSA needed that information. When she asked she said the word "Deductible". I stopped her right there and let her know that she does not have traditional insurance and the lingo is completely different. I told her that she has and IUA of $1500. She did not know what I was talking about. I explained that is stands for Initial Unshared Amount. That is what traditional insurance would call a deductible. Once I explained that she asked if there was some sort of form that we could send her that says all of that just in case the people or whomever needed it when trying to open an HSA. I was not sure so I asked Patti. She said no not really and I put the call back to her to better explain some things to Bergen. Patti let her know the full detail on the type of plan that she has because her plan is actually HSA compatible. She explained that with this type of plan that she has she can get an HSA through us and not have to go to some other type of bank or what not. Patti told her that with the plan the reason it is compatible is because the MEC that she has(APEX/RCI) is for high deductible. Bergen has member and family so her "High Deductible" is for $6000. She has that but does not technically use that. Because she has Sedera with her IUA of the $1500, which is better and less confusing that using the high deductible of the $6000. Patti said that her MEC is for Preventative ONLY, but could also be used for Injury/Illness, which is what the $6000 is for. But that is why we don''t mention that because it is so high and makes things a lot harder. That is why we have the Sedera aspect for diagnostic. It was a little confusing to explain to Bergen but Patti did a great job and Bergen was not confused at all by the end of the conversation. Bergen is all set and can open the HSA that she called in trying to do. -KF/PB', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-02 12:42:39', '2019-10-02 12:42:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041577015', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Acct set up fee charged and billing set up to start 10/22. Good to go for 11/1', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-10-02 12:41:39', '2019-10-02 12:41:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041610003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041906068', 'Sue Lepping', NULL, '10-2-19 Sue is 56, healthy, quit her job and is working on getting her real estate license now. Ins ended Sept. 30 but has Cobra as backup if need be.  No tobacco, meds for menopause, progesterone and estrogen, plus zoloft citraline. Send her vision option! Likes the $1000 / $350 Redirect option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-10-02 12:20:25', '2019-10-02 12:20:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041607008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041599023', 'Amber Neumann', NULL, 'Amber called in and wanted to double check that we have the correct mailing address on file, because she took some sort of blood test for some sort of from through us? Which by the way I have never heard of that and I have absolutely no clue what she is talking about. Anyway when I read her address that we have on file here she said it was in correct and that is what is on her ID which is wrong. But I told her that we will be sending a Member Change Request Form to her right now and to fill it out ASAP because she will be getting a bunch of mail from us, Sedera, and ASI very very shortly. She needs to make sure she fills the change form out NOW! She also asked when should she cancel her Blue Shield Health Insurance because she has a November 1 start date with us. I told her at the end of the month to cancel with them right before she becomes active here. If she cancels now and god forbid something happens while she is waiting for this plan to be active she will be SOL for the time being. Patti is sending the Member Change Request Form to her right now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-02 11:49:15', '2019-10-02 11:49:15'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041594038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012064043', 'Rudolfo Ramirez', NULL, 'Was just notified by Mary Jo @ Lynwood that this member termed employment eff 8/31.  I will submit to Sedera &amp; ASi', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-02 11:19:52', '2019-10-02 11:19:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041607003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011740011', 'Kathleen VanGoethem', NULL, 'Kathleen called in and she needed some help finding providers in network and just had a few general questions. She needed me to look up for a Mammogram, she gave me the place she has used in the past and before I even looked it up I knew the name and I already knew they were in network. Invision Sally Jobe. She also is needing a few vaccines and all the ones she needs are indeed covered. I told her that she pays for it out of pocket but submits the bill/receipt to ASI and they will fully reimburse her. She asked how she goes about getting the Mammogram and Women''s Wellness Visit covered. I explained the card that she HAS to bring, which is her ASI card. She does have it. I explained how she presents herself. I let her know that I would be sending a few different emails to her that fully explains what she needs to do. I sent her the 2 list''s she needed, I sent her the link on how to look up providers herself if she would like in the future and that email has the 64+ Preventative Care services that are covered. I let her know to look at that attachment at the bottom of that specific email. i also sent her how to submit her bills to Sedera if she ever may have some sort of injury/illness. I let her know of everything that she needs to to make sure that she goes about everything the CORRECT way and that things will be covered as long as she follows the instructions. She seemed to understand everything I told her and she was very happy I was able to sit here and take the time to go over everything with her on the phone. She said most people just like to try and get all the info as quickly was possible and kick her off the phone. I said that would NEVER happen here, especially with me. I am MORE than happy to sit here and go over everything the correct way and make sure that she and ANY member fully understands what to do with none to very very very minimal mistakes. No body is perfect. But I let her know that this is not a place where we do not care about our members. In fact, the complete opposite. We truly and deeply care about our members and their health. All we want to do is make sure that everyone is ok and that everyone is happy, satisfied, and just fully knows how to live a much healthier and better life! Kathy was VERY happy to hear all this and very happy that is was actually very easy to get this done. She looks forward to hearing from me and being able to get everything started and get to her appointments. I ALSO send her the www.healthgrades.com website because for the OBGYN list that I looked up there was 275 results. SO I told her about the health grades website so she can look up some reviews on the providers before just making an appointment so she can feel better about who she is going to see and safe. She was very very much enthralled that I would send her that and let her know how to make her feel a LOT better about everything. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-10-02 11:15:39', '2019-10-02 11:15:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041594033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010059065', 'Mary Kirby', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request I will cancel ASi &amp; Sedera &amp; FTNI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-02 10:32:38', '2019-10-02 10:32:38'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041594028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032679315', 'Robert Neufeld', NULL, 'Member called in letting me know that son might have broken his arm and didn''t know what to do next.  I went through what he had to do.  He said his wife was nervous about $5000 IUA wanted to know if he could change that.  I advised him no not until next year when plan renews.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-10-02 10:19:27', '2019-10-02 10:19:27'),
