  ('zcrm_1579374000041019003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028459022', 'Liat Lieberman Tabachnik', NULL, 'Jennifer at RCI explained that all of the testing done at the ENT is not covered- it didn''t qualify as a "lab test".  Wendy has asked Dave Shull to provide us with a list of exclutions so that we can give them to the members. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-18 07:53:48', '2019-09-18 07:53:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031420417', 'Taylor Hildreth', NULL, 'I tried giving Taylor a call to help guide her through the process but it went to voicemail, I left a very long detailed message on what she needs to do in this situation and urging her to go to the ER if she feels as though that is the right thing for her child.  Again- cash pay nothing more than $500 IUA, ask to be billed for the rest.  Ask for the detailed medical receipt so that you can open up a need with Sedera.- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 18:23:25', '2019-09-17 18:23:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031420417', 'Taylor Hildreth', NULL, 'a staff member from an Urgent Care called in stating that one of Tayor''s children was there, in bad shape and needed to be seen.  I explained what type of plan Taylor has and told her that she is cash pay up until her $500 mark, and to be billed anything over that $500 - the woman asked if there was anyway that we could see if she had at least met part of that $500, I told her, no...that unlike a deductible, this system is per need that if the child had seen the doctor yesterday for the same illness that any of that money would then go towards the amount.  The lady said that she would speak to Taylor about this. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 18:15:01', '2019-09-17 18:15:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040995011', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041020063', 'Mitchell Bloom', NULL, '9-17-19 Enrolling now as 2 separate memberships for the DPC membership. Mitch alone and Amy and son and daughter on other membership. $402/$1500, $339/$1500 = $741 and with Harmony Health. Plus $180 for DPC entire family.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-09-17 16:18:10', '2019-09-17 16:18:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005663233', 'Jason Lewis', NULL, 'Jason wanted to know what to do because his dentist found something "he didn''t like" in the back of Jason''s throat.  He wanted to know what to do to ensure that the procedure to remove it and send it for biopsy would be covered by liberty.  I told him that Liberty probably is not going to mind BUT he needs to speak with someone there that can help solidify what he needs to do. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 16:16:33', '2019-09-17 16:16:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000026209114', 'Kelly Shafer', NULL, 'Kelly said that the staff at her mammogram facility told her that they wouldn''t take her card I told her that I would try and see if this facility was in network, her doctor as well.  Both were.  Kelly is always extremely uninterested in how her plan works....but I went through it all again anyway.  I sent her the script. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 15:48:34', '2019-09-17 15:48:34'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011809121', 'Annette Wolf', NULL, 'Annette called in to ask about the need limit per year for her and her husband- she got a little flustered but not mad when I was trying to explain this to her- she then apologized saying it''s all just so confusing.   I told her that we understand that the plan can be difficult to wrap your mind around and that''s why we are here to answer all the questions she has....then I offered to help get some of her meds priced. She was thankful for all of the help! - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 15:21:05', '2019-09-17 15:21:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000041007003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000031420287', 'Payson McElveen', NULL, 'Payson called to see if the doctor he had an appointment with for an MRI right now, I had a really hard time finding the doctor because he gave me the name misspelled- after a bit of him getting frustrated and saying "well I''m just going to do it" and "I was told that pretty much everybody takes this insurance"  "am I right?"  long story short Payson didn''t like the fact that I was taking this more seriously than he was.  I told him that I would keep searching- in the mean time he could call the office and use the script I sent him.  I asked when this apt was and he said pretty soon....I told him that just because the doctor is in network it doesn''t mean that the facility where he is getting the MRI is.  I tried to go over the needs process with Sedera if needed but he was talking down to me "so I need to make a call before I can get this done?" again, annoyed.  This is an older injury, that his sponser Red Bull (he is a professional cyclist) is helping him with. I am not sure, but I did give him all the info he needed to hear- now we wait and see if he took my advice. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-17 14:58:55', '2019-09-17 14:58:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000022038146', 'Paul Suggett', NULL, 'Paul sent in a MEC Provider Billing Help Form. He wrote in the comment section:
My daughter had a fever of 103.2 yesterday and had trouble swallowing. We took her to the nearest Urgent Care. I was told my plan gave us three $50 urgent care co-pays per year. The facility said they had never worked with this insurance and were going to bill us at the full price. They also said they will bill for additional services beyond the $150 and took a credit card. Can you help us sort this out please?

I sent him an email asking if the facility was in network and if he called here before the appointment to make sure. I looked up the name of the facility and even out to 100 miles there was nothing, so I assume not and that is why he is being billed. He also only attached 2 receipts, not actual bills. I told him to get the EOB the detailed medical bill with the CPT codes on the bill and send it over to me. I also asked for him to send me the address with the zip code so I can look that up in out in network website. I told him the network is called the PHCS Network. I am waiting for a response from him will all the info that will be needed. Once I get all that then I can send everything out to APEX/RCI and get a support case started for him. I let Kelly Cheever know what was going on so if he calls or emails she will know what is going on and let her know I am leaving this note for her to see as well. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 14:42:41', '2019-09-17 14:42:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011752474', 'Eric Fields', NULL, 'Wendy called in and had to transfer Eric over to me, for some reason he was not able to get through to my phone for some reason. He needed some help with hoe to upload some bills and receipts over to Sedera. He said that he has already started the process with someone over at Sedera but he forgot how to go about. I asked him is he was assigned a case worker from Sedera and he said not that he could remember. I let him know that since he has already started something with Sedera that he needs to contact the, because they are a separate vendor then us here at MPowering and I would not have access to any of his files with them. I gave him Sedera''s phone number and I also told him I would send an email that explains how to submit bill to Sedera. He was very grateful with the information I gave him and that I was a great help with sending the email as well instead of just pushing him off to Sedera. I told him that the email will also have Sedera''s info in there as well and a list of instructions step by step to help him and walk him through with ease. Very happy for the help :) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 12:48:25', '2019-09-17 12:48:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039539039', 'Robert Mitchell', NULL, 'Marjorie called in and she needed help with submitting a receipt she has for something that is injury/illness. I told her that with her plan Redirect that they are ALWAYS going to be her first point of contact. I gave her their phone number and I also told her that if Redirect does not pick up to try calling Sedera. I explained who Sedera is and that with anything that is non preventative, injury/illness that Sedera is who she would need to contact and send bills and receipts into. I said call Redirect first and if they don''t answer to try calling Sedera. She was happy with the information I gave her. I am going to send her an email that explains how she submits bills over to Sedera. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 12:35:13', '2019-09-17 12:35:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005030392', 'Deborah Badgley', NULL, 'Deb requested a cancellation form to fill out so she can cancel. She stated that she has been trying to get a colonoscopy paid for for almost "3 years". She said she got a notice right after she was told everything was covered and paid for, from a collection agency and also being told that nothing was covered or paid. She then went to a doctors appointment on Thursday 9/13/19  and when she tried to call the number on her insurance card she could not reach anyone, it went straight to a voicemail stating that ASI was closed and to so she had to pay for that bill. She wanted to inquire about a reimbursement. She called in yesterday on 9/16/19 and she wanted to stop all payments and just cancel. She stated that it has been a never ending circle and everything that she has had to do has just been too much trouble and nothing seems to get solved. She went to her bank and told them to stop payment and then called me to cancel. I apologized greatly to her and told her that this usually doesn''t happen and that we are still going to work on her issues and get everything solved to the best of our abilities. John gave her a call today and is dealing with the issues she has. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 12:31:48', '2019-09-17 12:31:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007027003', 'Brent Cesare', NULL, 'Brent called in and stated that he is pretty sure that he called or emailed or however, to switch his card for the automatic payment but he got an email for "Pending Cancellation". He asked me if the old one was an Amex card. I told him I can not look into that but Sunny with finance will be able to, transferred to Sunny. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 12:11:01', '2019-09-17 12:11:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040978013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027654371', 'Valerie Igler', NULL, 'Received cancellation request from this member.  I will email Sedera &amp; cancel in RCI portal and cancel pmt in FTNI.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-09-17 12:03:17', '2019-09-17 12:03:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040995003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041020161', 'Joshua Duffy', NULL, '9-17-19 Karen is enrolling now in PDHC for herself and then her 2 kids will be separate on PDHC with Redirect which she will pay for also. They file taxes independently. She wants them to have access to unlimited PCP $289/$500.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-09-17 11:28:52', '2019-09-17 11:43:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040993003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005653245', 'Michel Abboud', NULL, 'Called in and was confused why he had a cancellation email sent to him when "a couple months ago I called in and changed my credit card number to a different and only one of the payments came out this month and not the other, and now I was sent a cancellation email. Why is that, what is going on?" I told him that I would transfer him to Sunny with the finance department because she is the one that would deal with this situation. I transferred to Sunny and she looked him up and she said there was no cancellation email sent to him. He had spoken to Kelly Cheever and apparently he did not want to fill out the form for updating information. She took the call and is speaking with Michel now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 11:24:53', '2019-09-17 11:24:53'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040986003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881027', 'John Dooley', NULL, 'Welcome call complete. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-09-17 10:21:43', '2019-09-17 10:21:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040978008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021919309', 'Kristi Lewis', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request.  I will cancel with Sedera &amp; FTNI &amp; in RCI portal', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-09-17 10:08:45', '2019-09-17 10:08:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040978003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037141256', 'John Phibbs', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request I will cancel with Sedera &amp; RCI via portal.  Also cancel billing in FTNI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-09-17 09:44:30', '2019-09-17 09:44:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040965008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000006151231', 'Steven Salyers', NULL, 'PB- Member called in requesting cancellation I will send out form', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-09-17 08:48:29', '2019-09-17 08:48:29'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040939101', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000040874041', 'Robert McCord', NULL, 'Acct set up charged 9/17, billing will start 9/20. Good to go for a 10/1 start', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-09-17 08:28:10', '2019-09-17 08:28:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040965003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028459022', 'Liat Lieberman Tabachnik', NULL, 'called in asking about why she is being billed for services even when having the copay plan.  I asked her to take pictures of everything she is looking at and to send everything to me so that I can send it to Jennifer at RCI to get some sort of explanation. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-09-16 17:40:57', '2019-09-16 17:40:57'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040939096', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041020063', 'Mitchell Bloom', NULL, '9-16-19 Mitch 60, Amy 47 and son 15. They are Jewish, healthy, athletes. He''s reading some bad reviews online for LHS and Medishare and a bit concerned. Someone from his Thincon or Sincon Group mentioned Sedera. He''s not sure who it was and I asked him to find out if possible. Amy is part of Cloud Medical already and son is not. Told him to find out how much it costs to add son since it''s definitely the most affordable route for Amy and Son at $339 / $1500. For Mitch it''s $507 / $1500 Redirect at age 60.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-09-16 17:13:59', '2019-09-16 17:13:59'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040939091', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000041020161', 'Joshua Duffy', NULL, '9-16-19 Karen is in 50''s and has two boys 19 and 22 turning 23 soon. No meds, no tobacco, healthy. Just one son with psychiatrist visits and meds for mental health. She likes the Redirect and boys PSDHC to encourage them to do annual wellness visits. $335/$1500 for her and $500/$269 for boys.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-09-16 16:30:42', '2019-09-16 16:30:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000040939086', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000051715135', 'Sylvia Theisen', NULL, '9-16-19 Sylvia is 59 and turning 60 on Oct. 7th. Not worried about locking in price at the 50''s age range. Will wait to ponder if she wants to switch from LHS to HEP. Redirect is best for her. Has hypothyroid issue managed with meds and depression meds. Looked at $1500 IUA Redirect $507. Asked about son and quoted her SDHC at $1500/$177 or $500/$203 since he doesn''t necessarily do his annual wellness visit. She may wait until the new year to switch. In no rush.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-09-16 15:26:28', '2019-09-16 15:26:28'),
