  ('zcrm_1579374000039569013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039575047', 'Samuel Mitchell', NULL, '8-12-19 Sam is 5 in 2019 and has asthma that is too risky to put him on HEP. So they chose an Anthem Silver plan for $494.55 a month with a $2000 or so ded. starting 9/1/19', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-08-13 20:30:06', '2019-08-13 20:39:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000039526043', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011779665', 'Jason Reynolds', NULL, 'Jason called to ask about the process he would need to go through to get a few cardiac and imaging tests done.  I asked him how this was prompted and he told me that his close friend died after running a marathon last weekend and wanted to make sure that he was healthy and well so that he didn''t have to be worried about his own health.  I asked if he had spoken to a doctor about this and he said no.  I told him that he would need to get scripts from his doctor so that Sedera could use their lookup tool to find the best rate''s and facilities for him to get these tests done.  But told him that this would be an out of pocket expense and not something that Sedera would share in if his doctor didn''t think that these tests were medically warranted.  He understood, I told him that Sedera could help find the facilities involved though, but that they would need the CPT codes to do so.  I sent him the provider lookup, 5 ways to avoid bills @ preventive care screening, Sedera''s phone number in the needs email. I told him that he could call back anytime if he had more questions. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-08-13 19:48:06', '2019-08-13 19:48:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000039569008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000042696258', 'Joanne Mielnick', NULL, '8-13-19 She''s 62 and divorced on Cobra ''til Dec. 1st. Looked at Indiv options after Cobra ends and it''s going to be $1400/$7900 through Kaiser! She''s retired and no tobacco. Only pre-x is blood pressure meds low dose. She''s a competitive ballroom dancer and broke wrist a few months ago. It''s all set now but the cost at Swedish Medical was $60K!!!  She paid $2600. Also paying $35 a month for dental but told her may not be worth it with individual plans.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-08-13 16:31:10', '2019-08-13 16:31:10'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000039526038', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038087012', 'Jonathan McCallister', NULL, 'Welcome call completed.  Jonathan stated that his broker went over medical cost sharing so that he understood.  I gave a brief definition of that as well.  He was biking home from work, he said that he didn''t have computer access but he uses his phone for that, he was fine with me going over everything and sending him all of the emails that corresponded to our conversation. Jonathan sounds like the perfect MPowering member- he rides his bike 2 hours a day too and from work, and he is very upbeat.  He said that he understood everything on the call. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-08-13 16:27:36', '2019-08-13 16:27:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000039569003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001881027', 'John Dooley', NULL, '8-13-19 Just completed enrollment for Redirect with $1000/$350. He just has one ongoing medication and otherwise healthy. Good to go!', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-08-13 15:21:17', '2019-08-13 15:21:17'),
