  ('zcrm_1579374000038067028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012724403', 'Fletcher Otwell', NULL, 'Fletcher called to update his payment method, he was in front of a computer so I guided him to the form and let him know that finance would get it tomorrow and make those changes. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 19:32:17', '2019-07-11 19:32:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038067023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000005544375', 'Bradley Brown', NULL, 'called to cancel, sent him form. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 18:16:25', '2019-07-11 18:16:25'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038067018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000008973029', 'Julian Gonzalez-Becerra', NULL, 'he called in to request his "policy information" emailed to him.  I told him that someone at home office would have to help him with that and emailed Patti to help. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 17:11:05', '2019-07-11 17:11:05'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050044', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038529382', 'Mitchell Magdovitz', NULL, '7-11-19 Fox is 37, family healthy, no meds, except IUD, no tobacco. Needs Aug. 1st start date. Kicked off CHP+ bc earning too much. Doesn''t like the idea of paying and getting reimbursed. Redirect seems best for them! Has lots of questions and wanted to read reviews that don''t exist. Sending her link to click funnel to learn more and to be prepared for Monday''s appt.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 16:47:12', '2019-07-11 16:47:12'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038067013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000025389081', 'Kelly Mills', NULL, 'Kelly called in because she went to an eye surgeon complaining of "floaters" in her eyes- the doctor checked her out and told her that all was well.  But they said that they couldn''t use her eye insurance because this wasn''t preventative.  They did end up taking the card, and I did end up finding the doctor as in network.  I told her that they probably just billed RCI, and that in the end she will only owe $50.  I sent her the chart going over all of her co-pay benefits, emailed her the provider network search, and Sedera videos because she admittedly keeps forgetting how the program works. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 16:41:48', '2019-07-11 16:41:48'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038070008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028419015', 'Daryl Morris', NULL, '07.11.19:  I called MPB and spoke w/Kelly Cheever about the issue.  She said she will call Jennifer and will discuss the issue w/Guy to try and resolve it.  Will get back to me.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2019-07-11 16:30:09', '2019-07-11 16:30:09'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038070003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028419015', 'Daryl Morris', NULL, '07.10.19:  Daryll called. Said she had a colonoscopy: had thoroughly checked w/her doctor, the facility, MPB and Sedera to be certain she would not have to pay any fees for this procedure.  Everyone said she would not.  She recently got a letter from the facility telling her she''s 90 days overdue on a $600 fee for the facility.  She spoke w/Kelly F. who sent her to Jennifer Chastine of 
RCI/Apex, who found out the facility is out of her network.  Daryl said they told her it was in network when she had the procedure done.  I told her I would look into it and get back to her.', 'Joan Phelps', 'Joan Phelps', '2019-07-11 16:28:42', '2019-07-11 16:28:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050039', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000039613005', 'David Anderson', NULL, '7-11-19 Dave is 41, wife is 37, 4 kids! Exploring all 5 options. Told him Co-Pay network might be going away soon. His daughter''s leukemia was 5 years ago. She gets checked 1x per year as preventative measure. He knows that is his responsibility to pay for those annual checks. He believes his daguther''s leukemia won''t come back or anything stemming from it. I told him not a good idea for his daughter but he doesn''t agree. Says her chance of it coming back are the same for her as everyone else now that we''re at the 5 year point. Son has seen dermatologist for pimples and knows may need to pay for that on his own if comes back.  I told him to check all medical records of all family members to make sure there''s nothing on there that he''s not aware of. He''s not concerned but I expressed my concerns many times. Sounds like he will check medical records after I told him to contact his doctors to access them. He''s moving Aug. 1st to UT and coverage ending Aug. 1st. Told him the deadline is July 20th. He says his family goes to the dr. about 1x each per year. His current employer plan is incredible with $0 deductible and co-pays and labs at great prices but new employer doesn''t have a good offering. He will ponder and let me know what he chooses.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 16:27:24', '2019-07-11 16:27:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050034', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036193007', 'Bradley Jahnke', NULL, 'Clickfunnel completed....marketing materials completed....left message to call him to follow up with implementation.', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2019-07-11 15:38:03', '2019-07-11 15:38:03'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038067008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028419015', 'Daryl Morris', NULL, 'latest from Jennifer @ RCI- Kelly,

 

Yes I did get the information back that it is still not in network however I was able to get it sent back to be reprocessed and paid per the plan documents. There is a small part that states if no choice of a network provider, plans will be paid as though an in network one.

I have called the member as well and let her know of this.

 

Have a wonderful day.

 

Jennifer', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 15:36:00', '2019-07-11 15:36:00'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038067003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000014508197', 'Jose Ernesto Rodriguez aleman', NULL, 'Megan Miller from Sedera reached out via Slack to state that  Johanna had called them asking about a rate change.  I called Johanna and let her know that I would be happy to go over the rate changes, letter and emails that were sent to her and that I would be available until 10 est. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-07-11 15:31:41', '2019-07-11 15:31:41'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037008015', 'Kellie Whitney', NULL, '7-11-19 Wendy Varble is the DPC Dr. in Buena Vista called Peace of Mind Medical Care. She will join by Aug. 1st and show proof of membership. Kellie was referred to Sedera by her broker who does not do MCS stuff, only trad. Enrollment complete $1500/$230 DPC.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 15:14:52', '2019-07-11 15:27:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '7-11-19 Rachel just completed the Referring Entity form to market this to her WWSRA Assoc with 85-950 active members. They will roll this out as we approach the upcoming winter season while folks are preparing and have time to look at this. We are waiting for Click Funnel to be built and admin stuff to be complete for next steps.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 14:34:36', '2019-07-11 14:34:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032454006', 'Georgannna Garrison', NULL, 'Cami Flores is the name she goes by.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 14:32:26', '2019-07-11 14:32:26'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038058003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012594106', 'Sharon Carducci', NULL, 'Member called in very upset because she had been advised by Jan to do the following:
1. Remove her husband(who is 67) from plan via HRA that was submitted on deadline of 6/17
2. Also that we would refund her the difference of her overcharge. 
We were never informed of any of this.  I reached out to Jan and have yet to hear back from her.
I have refunded her the difference of the price and will inform carriers to take spouse off plan', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-07-11 13:52:30', '2019-07-11 13:52:30'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038050003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000038087106', 'Jennifer Mangin', NULL, '7-11-19 Enrolled in DPC at $5000 IUA. Understands it''s per incident and 5 max for family. Has DPC for small stuff and really never goes to dr. bc they are super healthy.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-07-11 13:25:18', '2019-07-11 13:25:18'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038041003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000007278037', 'Richard Wrightsman', NULL, 'Richards Fiance called in because Richard has been throwing up for the last 2 days straight. She is very worried about him and he said that he doesn''t think he can just go to a regular doctor and sit and wait because of the constant throwing up and wants to go to the E.R. She as calling to see what to do and what we recommend. I told her that with this type of situation is it an injury/illness and that is when his IUA of $1000 comes into play. That is what he is going to be responsible for out of pocket. This is not something that will be covered. She fully understood and so does he on what that entails. I let her know that if the bill is anymore than his IUA he is to ask the provider to bill him the rest. Richard will then need to contact Sedera asap and let them know what is going on. I explained to her who Sedera was and what they do when is comes to submitting a "Need". I told her that unfortunately with his situation, at least in my personal opinion with experience with this type of sickness, that the bill is most likely going to be over her IUA and to contact Sedera now and let them know a head of time to start the process before it gets complicated and to let Sedera know where they are going and what for. I let them know that we TRY( unless it is a severe or truly a situation that NEEDS the E.R.) to have them avoid the hospital and go to an Urgent Care facility. The Urgent Care places are usually way less expensive and the urgent care place will defiantly be able to assist them with what is going on. While the Fiance was on the phone I looked up an Urgent Care facility around their address on the account. I found one that was actually very close she confirmed and was opening up in 15 minutes from that time I was on the phone with them, which makes it a lot better because they would not have to be sitting and waiting for hours. The Fiance was extremely grateful for all of my help that I was able to provide for her. She was almost in tears with how happy I made her and Richard feel that we actually are a company that truly cares about their member. I reassured her that of yes of course we care. WE are here to make  sure that our members are taken care of and happy with what we have to offer.  That is our goal here and our number 1 priority. She felt a lot more at ease and not as panicked. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-07-11 12:52:50', '2019-07-11 12:52:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000038009026', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000015979037', 'Ryan Nelson', NULL, 'Bailey called in and was calling in regards to her husband Ryan. She stated that every time she has gone into her children''s yearly wellness visit and hands the front desk her ASI card that they are being told they no longer have benefits and are not members. I spoke with Patti and asked why that might be because they clearly are still members and have not cancelled. Patti saw that their start date was May 1st of 2018 and during that time these members had HMA and were switched over to ASI. Patti had me make sure that Bailey was using the ASI card and not using their old HMA card. When I asked Bailey this she said she 100% is using their ASI card every time and was holding the card right in front of her as we were on the phone just now. She said in big letters is clearly says ASI. Bailey told me they do not even have any cards at all that say HMA. SO I told Bailey that there should be absolutely no reason at all that they are being told they are not members or have no benefits. I told her that she needs to contact ASI right away because that is an issue on ASI''s end. She was very sweet and was very thankful for the help that I gave her and the confirmation that they indeed do have benefits and it says NO WHERE on her account here that she is cancelled or has no benefits. I provided her with ASI''s phone number and is calling them right now. If I hear back from her or ASI I will be sure to update notes with all information provided. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-07-11 12:23:28', '2019-07-11 12:23:28'),
