  ('zcrm_1579374000037968023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036932155', 'Amy Betancourt', NULL, 'Left a detailed message on voicemail. Sent email to book online the 15 minute welcome call. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-07-10 10:36:23', '2019-07-10 10:36:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000037974003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018819248', 'Linda Pan', NULL, 'Left message for Linda', 'MPB Health Member Notification', 'MPB Health Member Notification', '2019-07-10 10:34:14', '2019-07-10 10:34:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000037968018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037016068', 'Mary Heiberger', NULL, 'Spoke to member will book online the 15 minute welcome call. Sent email to do so. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-07-10 10:32:14', '2019-07-10 10:32:14'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000037973003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032104142', 'Judy Van Acker', NULL, 'Judy called in and she needed a run down and overview of what she needs to do to go and have an annual wellness visit and how it is covered. Pretty much how her plan works. She was very patient with me and very nice. She did not get frustrated at all. I spoke with her for 20 minutes about how her entire plan works with both preventative  and diagnostic injury/illness. I explained that for anything preventative she needs to call in or look up on the Multi Plan website that the provider she has chosen is in network and if not than to look up what type of provider she is looking for in her area and it will bring up a list and she can choose any one of them on the list. I told her that she will need to have her RCI card for when she goes in and I explained a few examples of what preventative services are covered and available. She does have her RCI card with her handy. She told me she did make sure the provider was in network and I double checked for her just in case and he is indeed in network. I told her how she is going to present herself with her card and what to say word for word. I told her that she needs to make sure that if she wants it to be 100% covered that she needs to let her provider know it is strictly preventative. I let her know though that if she does have any symptoms of any kind or any sort of pain and she brings it up during the visit that she is going to be responsible our of pocket for a portion of her bill or possibly the whole bill. It all depends on how the provider does her billing. She 100% understood that and was fine with it. I then got into the diagnostic portion of her plan and injury/illness. I gave her a few examples of what that entails, IE, surgery of sorts, falling and breaking her arm, bad back pain, anything that will have to do with god forbid going to the emergency room, ect.. I explained that that is when her IUA of $5000 kicks in. I told her that she does NOT pay anything over that or getting reimburse can be a bit tricky and makes the process harder. I told her once she meets her IUA she is to be asked to be billed the rest and then she gets in contact with Sedera. I fully explained who Sedera is and what they do when it comes to submitting her bills to start a "Need". Judy was EXTREMELY happy with all this information that I gave her and her exact words at the end of the call were "I am finally fully understanding how all of this works and you have been a HUGE help for me and my husband. We were very confused before we called in and now we truly understand what we have and love it even more. Thank you so much Kelly!" Judy and her husband seem to really get what we do here and how their plan works in full. I let her know that I will be sending all this info via emails with a few templates. How to present herself, how to submit her bills to Sedera and start a "need", how to do a provider search at home, and lastly the 64+ list of preventative services that are approved by the ACA. Very very happy member now!! -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-07-10 10:27:43', '2019-07-10 10:27:43'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000037968013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000037016117', 'Katie Craig', NULL, 'Spoke to member booked her 15 minute welcome call for Friday, July 12, 2019 at 9:00 a.m. mountain time/ 11:00 a.m. eastern time. Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', 'Vanessa Orozco', '2019-07-10 10:10:54', '2019-07-10 10:10:54'),
