  ('zcrm_1579374000037031013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028257159', 'Michele Schwadron', NULL, 'Michele called in and was asking why she has gotten a bill in the mail for her annual physical. She explained that she thought she was able to go to any doctor of her choosing except when it comes to a Mammogram. I explained to her that that is incorrect and for preventative services like her annual wellness visit, colonoscopy screening, women''s wellness visit, ect.. that she HAS to go to a provider/facility that is in network with the PHCS network. If she does not go to a provider in network she is then responsible out of pocket for whatever the bill may be and it will not go towards  her IUA. I explained to her what he IUA is and how that works, along with submitting bills to Sedera if she has any sort of injury/illness. I sent her the email that explains how she submits her bills and starts a "Need" with Sedera when the time comes. She understood and was not upset in anyway. She said she will just pay the bill and go to a provider for another physical that is in network because the doctor she went to recommended blood work to be done, so she doesn''t want to risk that blood work not be covered as well since it was recommend from the provider that was not in network. She then asked if I can find her providers for a General Practitioner, a mammogram, and a colonoscopy specialists. I told her I will be happy to help with that and will get those lists over to her ASAP. She was very very thrilled with all the information that I provided her and she said I was a HUGE help to her today. Very satisfied member now. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-06-20 12:39:08', '2019-06-20 12:39:08'),
