  ('zcrm_1579374000036922028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017830168', 'Laura Zaunbrecher', NULL, 'Laura called in and asked if her husband was successfully on boarded to the program- I told her yes.  She asked to go over "pre approval" or whatever she does need to do to get her husband an MRI.  I asked about the story behind that, what he needed an MRI for.  She told me that he has been having hip pain for the last few months.  I asked if he had seen a doctor yet, she said no.  I told her that if Sedera was to help them find a lower cost facility they would need the exact CPT code that the doctor would script.  She said that he needed the MRI AND HOPEFULLY he doesn''t need to have surgery on it.  I told her that the first step would be to find a doctor, and asked if she had anyone in mind.  She said yes, it would be a chiropractor by the name of Richy Hanson, she said "yeah, maybe we should speak to him first" I told her that Sedera has a 3 year look back for any symptoms or diagnosis, and that this may not be considered a sharable expense.  She said "oh, well, it definitely happened after the first of April"  I told her that her husband should go to the doctor and get a doctors opinion before they both jump to a conclusion of MRI and possible surgery.  After that if that is something that their doctor wants to do, then she needs to call Sedera straight away let them know what is going on and let them decide if this is a sharable need or not.  I sent her many many emails with info related to Sedera.  She also had a swarm of questions about preventative care that I answered for her and sent educational emails on that subject as well, she was thrilled that there was a script for her!  and that I took the time to answer so many questions.  I will be sharing these notes with Dania as well as Guy.  - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-06-17 11:39:47', '2019-06-17 11:39:47'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036936028', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012594156', 'Arthur Schwadron', NULL, 'Spoke with Art and he is aware of the compliance issue and will address shortly. He did say that his email regarding the rate change reflected that his ex-wife seemed to still be on the plan. He is going to make an outbound call to remedy. He is aware and ok with his rate increase.', 'Kyle Sheehan', 'Kyle Sheehan', '2019-06-17 11:36:32', '2019-06-17 11:36:32'),
