  ('zcrm_1579374000036706008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018819577', 'Nanci Alpert', NULL, 'Pmt update in FTNI - Renewal 2019', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-06-12 07:46:06', '2019-06-12 07:46:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036706003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033336100', 'Jack Lipton', NULL, 'Per an email from Kevin Michaels zip code was entered wrong on the application.  Only place I found that was wrong was in Selerix.  I let Elizabeth know this to update.', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-06-12 07:09:31', '2019-06-12 07:09:31'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036687003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000023592249', 'Gregory Meell', NULL, 'Spoke to Greg....getting his colonoscopy....setting up welcome call for June 17, 2019.', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2019-06-11 18:15:58', '2019-06-11 18:15:58'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036673010', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000023592249', 'Gregory Meell', NULL, 'This very nice member just called in with NO WELCOME call, NO education via email of ANY kind asking how he was going to get his APEX card that was never sent because his address was wrong!  I checked to see if dr and facility were in network and they are....but I told him that he needed to check with Guy about this.  I told him that I would request that a card be sent.  But he litteraly knows nothing and his colonoscopy is scheduled tomorrow.  Guy is going to call him- KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-06-11 17:48:40', '2019-06-11 17:48:40'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036673005', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000018819577', 'Nanci Alpert', NULL, 'Nanci called in to change her IUA, so I guided her to the link in her email. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-06-11 16:36:44', '2019-06-11 16:36:44'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036676003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036757110', 'Brandon Lowitz', NULL, '6-11-19 Brandon 49 turning 50 in Dec. 2019, wife 46 and twins 14. Brandon takes cholesterol meds, Lyrica and Lipitor. Lyrica costs $400+ on Goodrx. Will find out through World Meds. Takes 300mg 2x daily, 60 pills at 150 mg each. Has colonoscopy scheduled for Aug as preventative. Had 1 years ago. He was sick this year and hospitalized for 2 nights, 3 days and they never found out what''s wrong, no dianosis, decided maybe a bronchial issue. Explained pre-x many times over in case history to colonoscopy as non-preventative. He said it''s preventative. He''s paying $2750 now for Cobra for his entire family! Wants to do this for July 1st if he can read enough and feel comfortable before he leaves country after Friday.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-06-11 16:35:33', '2019-06-11 16:35:33'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036665003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036377058', 'Parker Thompson', NULL, '6-11-19 Explained to Aisha how membership works. They had a plan with UHC through Parker''s work that was costing $1000+ a month but supposedly only a $100 ded! They are planning to have another baby within the next year or so. They are talking about switching back to traditional ins if they do have another baby for ease of use and low ded. Told them to pay attention to when their open enrollment is for work. They can switch back if need be if decide to have baby. She doesn''t like the idea of birthing center bc she wants an epidural. Therefore, they would need $5K to pay for birth. Not psyched about that.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-06-11 14:52:52', '2019-06-11 14:52:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036662008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011610171', 'Melinda Grabau', NULL, 'Spoke to Mindy about situation with Midtown declining her procedure.  Informed client that I sent email re her problem with Midtown and their conversation with her.  Informed client that MD office will try and find another facility to get colonoscopy.  Client will call MD office to find out which facility to go to...waiting on call back from client.', 'Guy Travis', 'Guy Travis', '2019-06-11 14:46:46', '2019-06-11 14:46:46'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036664008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011899490', 'Savannah Jones', NULL, 'Savannah Jones husband, Austin, called in with many questions surrounding the rate increase and potentially adjusting the IUA that Savannah has- also he had a question about "pausing" or canceling her coverage.  I told him where to find the cancellation form as well as told him that they could call in anytime and we would send them a form. He thanked me for all of my help. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-06-11 14:40:36', '2019-06-11 14:40:36'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036664003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011509065', 'Joy Kelley', NULL, 'Joy called in pretty anxious about the letter she received from us about pre-authorization on preventative care.  I explained that this would be in regards to the "bigger ticketed" services such as colonoscopy and mammagram.  I looked up her kids pediatrician as well as her gyneo and found them in network- I told her to give us a call later in the year if her dr scripts her a mammagram so that we can make sure that all entities involved are in network and that the it is scripted as preventive rather than diagnostic. She was happy for all of the help, I told her to expect many emails from me going over some tips on preventative care. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-06-11 14:25:16', '2019-06-11 14:25:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036639033', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000027924115', 'Michael Henninger', NULL, 'called in and his son has a cyst on his arm that needs to be removed. Called back and spoke with Mike. He has not needed to use his plan yet since he has enrolled about 6 months ago so he did not know what to do. I explained with what is going on with his son that that would be considered injury/illness. He does not need to be in network and can call and go to any provider of his choosing. He asked what type of provider would deal with a cyst on the arm that needs to be removed and I recommended he use Teladoc and he said that he is already registered and ready to go. I told him instead of having to go to 2 different doctors, cut out the 1st visit to use Teladoc and they can recommend what to do and where to go without an extra charge. I also told him about how he is going to be using his IUA which is $1500. Anything after that is submitted to Sedera. I told him on how to submit his bills and gave him their phone number and sent the email that explains on how to submit. He was EXTREMELY happy with how I helped him. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-06-11 12:58:24', '2019-06-11 12:58:24'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036640006', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862222', 'Christopher Morano', NULL, 'Member submitted cancellation request.  I will notify Sedera ASi &amp; cancel FTNI', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-06-11 12:26:35', '2019-06-11 12:26:35'),
