  ('zcrm_1579374000036142008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012024293', 'Brian Johnson', NULL, 'I have reached out to Leena and Salena AGAIN today and asked for the latest on this claim.  I am not going to be sending Brian an email update because I have sent him so many, so far.  This should be wrapped up by now....KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-30 14:50:02', '2019-05-30 14:50:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036144003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017243508', 'Julie Beitscher', NULL, '5-30-19 Julie is considering switching to Assoc to gain access to Provider Directed solution. They are already members of a DPC and not getting discounted rate. If they remain with DPC I''ll request for her. DPC is in Loveland which is 2 1/2 hours from Fairplay, 80440. Steve is in the clear for any pre-x according to them. DOB 12-23-57. They have retired and are not earning any money, living off savings now. Could go onto Medicaid but still considering HEP for freedom of choice to see Functional Drs. DPC route is cheapest. They are only paying $100 total a month for both of them. But, explained some of the wellness might not be included by their DPC. Just depends on what that DPC covers. If they won''t want to drive so far they will choose PDHC with Redirect. They like the unlimited PCP visits. Julie might switch from Select to Assoc to gain access to PDHC. Price difference is very little for many more benefits. To switch from Select to Access Julie will have to cancel current membership and then reapply to new. MUST notify Patti to make sure they inform Sedera to keep their pre-x term from original start date.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-30 14:39:18', '2019-05-30 14:41:42'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036141013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011862244', 'Andrew Racuch', NULL, 'Regina called in and she stated that she has gone way over her $500 IUA for physical therapy that she has been getting done weekly. I stopped her there and told her she is not to go over her IUA and that she needs to get in contact with Sedera ASAP! I told her when she is close to her IUA she needs to open up a "Need" with Sedera. She is calling them right now. This is in regards to an issue she is having with her knee. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-30 14:11:55', '2019-05-30 14:11:55'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036142003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028522170', 'Jonathan Carroll', NULL, 'Lauren''s claim form the cleveland clinic was not being processed correctly due to her going to an outpatient facility for preventative care.  Shelley made an exception and covered the bill.  Lauren''s next question was can the other family members go back to the same facility and still be covered by the exception, Shelley asked around and said that the other family members COULD go back to that facility and that there shouldn''t be any further problems. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-30 14:10:11', '2019-05-30 14:10:11'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036115008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000004971047', 'Jeff Myers', NULL, 'Finally got in touch with Jeff and processed June+late fee on 5/30', 'Vladislava Terziyska', 'Vladislava Terziyska', '2019-05-30 13:09:02', '2019-05-30 13:09:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036141008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000032601016', 'Meggan Kramer', NULL, 'Meggan called in just wondering how the procedure for the prescription quote''s work. I explained that there is a form I will send her and she will fill it out and once I receive it I will find her the best prices. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-30 12:17:16', '2019-05-30 12:17:16'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036141003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000013822002', 'Elizabeth James', NULL, 'Elizabeth called in to cancel with us because she got a new job. Sent cancellation form. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-30 12:16:56', '2019-05-30 12:16:56'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036094017', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000012630194', 'Frances Primus', NULL, 'Frances called in to get some general information on how her plan works with both preventive and injury/illness. She did not know that you have to use a doctor in network for anything that is preventative. She was trying to get her annual mammogram screening done and was told by her provider that it would cost her $250 out of pocket. I stopped her there and confirmed it was just the annual screening and I stated that as long as you have a provider that does that procedure in network than you do NOT have to pay out of pocket. That is only for something that is related to an injury or illness. Diagnostic in nature. She fully understood and I found a provider for her that goes mammography in her area. I sent her some emails with the how to submit bills to Sedera, how to present your MEC, the provider list, and the 64+ list on preventative services. She also asked if we can send her another 1095 B form because the one she got has her old address on it. I confirmed the address on file in the CRM is correct and it was. Will need to have another 1095 form sent out ASAP. She was very happy with the information provided and understands how to use her plan. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-30 10:50:09', '2019-05-30 10:50:09'),
