  ('zcrm_1579374000036096046', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011881495', 'Dennis Larratt', NULL, 'Dennis had reached out to Sedera earlier in the day in regards to having issues scheduling a preventative care visit. The office did not recognize him telling them that he had MPowering Benefits/ASI insurance.  I ended up calling the office and speaking to Anne one of the front desk supervisors if they accepted his plan....she said yes and told me to let Dennis know that when he presents his card to mention the PHCS network.  I sent all of this info to Dennis along with a script that he can use, he thanked me for all of the details I gave him as well. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-29 18:34:02', '2019-05-29 18:34:02'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036096041', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028257367', 'Marta Heston', NULL, 'Marta''s husband Nicholas called in wondering how to submit $8,400 worth of hospital medical bills to us.  He told me that he was told that they had a $1000 deductible and to call us and submit the bills to us.  I told him that that information was completely incorrect and then went over Marta''s IUA and a general overview on how they needed to proceed by opening up a need and submitting bills to Sedera.  Nicholas was upset that he was told about the deductible and said that he would be calling Darius himself.   I sent an email with link and instructions plus phone number on how to open up a need with Sedera, as well as sent all of Sedera''s educational videos.  Nicholas thanked me for all of the information and said that he would call Sedera after he spoke with his wife. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-29 15:51:06', '2019-05-29 15:51:06'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036096036', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000019362002', 'Deb Bear', NULL, 'Deb called in to make sure that the facility and doctors that she was finding were approved by us for her colonoscopy.  I asked if there was one in particular that she was looking at (facility) she said that there was but that it wasn''t showing up in network BUT 3 doctors that are associated with the facility ARE in network.  I told her that Guy Travis would probably need to dig a bit deeper into this to see how the billing would work in a situation like that.  I asked if we found that facility as a "no go" if she would like us to find a list of facilities and doctors that we would approved.  She stopped me to say that her doctor wanted her to go to that specific center because the Cologuard test that John Kach approved came back positive and that she wanted to take advantage of the screening colonoscopy that is included on her plan.  I told her that this screening would be considered diagnostic at that she would be going through Sedera and opening up a need with them.  I told her that she needed to speak with Sedera and let them know what is going on before this procedure and she told me that she would. She admittedly wanted to skirt the system and squeeze in a colonoscopy- I transferred her to Guy and sent her info on how to submit a need to Sedera. -KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-29 15:15:52', '2019-05-29 15:15:52'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036100008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000017243508', 'Julie Beitscher', NULL, '5-29-19 Julie wants to add her husband to membership. She is not compliant for 2019. She can refer her husband to the Assoc and become compliant herself. He''s 60 and should join Redirect as his best option.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-29 15:07:38', '2019-05-29 15:07:38'),
