  ('zcrm_1579374000036007013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000010990092', 'Andrea Perrault', NULL, 'Andrea called in to get some more information on this new pre-authorization for high priced preventative procedures. She told me that she already had an appointment for a colonoscopy for 2 weeks from now and wanted to know what to do. I looked up the facility and it is indeed in network. I then did a little research on pricing for the center and gave the facility a call to get an estimate of pricing. They roughly came up with about $1750.00 which is what we are looking for, nothing over or close to $2500.00. She was very very happy with me helping her and actually get a price ranger for because she had no clue going into this. I also discussed a little bit how her plan works and MAKE SURE she tells the provider that is it STRICTLY a preventative visit ONLY. She fully understood everything that I explained to her and was satisfied with the info given. -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-28 13:06:50', '2019-05-28 13:06:50'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036004163', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016038161', 'Karee Watson', NULL, 'Emp Only $1500 IUA', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-05-28 12:38:45', '2019-05-28 12:38:45'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036004158', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000016038161', 'Karee Watson', NULL, 'pmt updated in FTNI renewal 2019', 'Patti Baron', 'Patti Baron', '2019-05-28 12:38:23', '2019-05-28 12:38:23'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036007008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000020482108', 'Gina Schwichtenberg', NULL, 'Gina called in to just get a better understanding of how her plan works and asking for my help on how to look up a general practitioner and an OBGYN provider. She was confused on how the preventative and injury/illness worked and she did not know what an IUA is and how it works. I explained in full detail the type of preventative services that are covered, ie; annual wellness visit, annual woman''s visit, 1st mammogram screening, colonoscopy screening, ect. I explained to her what she has to do if she has a diagnostic visit or she has an injury/illness. She 100% understood everything that I have told her on how to use her IUA and what is it strictly for. She was very satisfied with the information given. I sent her 4 different emails, the 1st was the 64+ list of preventative services approved by the ACA, how to it bills over to Sedera when she has a "Need", how to present herself when she goes to the providers, and 2 lists of providers for a GP and a OBGYN. She said she looks forward to using her plan and getting started. She said she has a MUCH better understanding of how her plan works and what to do and what not to do. :) -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-28 12:31:37', '2019-05-28 12:31:37'),
