  ('zcrm_1579374000036012003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000028171274', 'Diane Thomason', NULL, 'I was called at about 1:25 by John asking if I had been in touch with this lady, and I said no but would be willing to call her.  Diane said that she only wanted to get in touch with me BECAUSE when she had called in last week frustrated that she couldn''t get in touch with Sedera????I fixed the problem right away??? so today when she couldn''t get a hold of her rep Lauren Whetstone again....she called us AGAIN....and thought that I could help do the same thing all over again??????   I don''t remember any of that, but whatever.  She''s all set, Sedera contacted her back with a different program that she needs to get done now????? she said that this has been a nightmare and asked if she wanted too?  how she could cancel.  I told her, she said that she wasn''t there yet but again "this has been a nightmare" and thanked me for my time.  -----note- I don''t remember any of this. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-28 12:19:01', '2019-05-28 12:19:01'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000035997023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000001653045', 'Mary Poole', NULL, 'My wife was a member of Liberty Healthshare since 2016, ending the health cost coverage in March of 2019.Initially to be a member she also had to pay a $50 per month payment to My Academy of Health Excellence. We continued to make this payment until we found out from Liberty Healthshare that Liberty had terminated their arrangement with the Academy in February, 2017 because Liberty was dissatisfied with the Academy''s performance. We continued paying the $50 per month through October of 2018 when we found out this payment was no longer necessary per Liberty.We contacted the Academy twice, most recently by phone on 4/22/19 with Jenny at 855 816 4650, and both times were told the Academy would not make any refunds. They claim they sent us an email in August, 2017 notifying us of this change, fully 6 months after Liberty says their business arrangement had ended. We never received any such email in any case and only found out that we did not have to pay the Academy in November 2018 during a routine call to Liberty. We never accessed any services from the Academy.By my accounting the Academy should refund us for 21 months of payments at $50 per month (February, 2017 through October, 2018) or $1050.Thank you for your attention to this matter
Product_Or_Service: wellness assistance
Order_Number: na -via Liberty
Account_Number: na - via Liberty

My response:
	
This member was automatically cancelled off of our plan when she reached medicare age via our internal audit process. Our addon services are not necessary for someone on medicare. This was the 1st time we spoke with this member. She was upset and confused because she had not cancelled. I explained that she was cancelled due to age. She confirmed that she was on medicare. The member refunded one month at that point as a courtesy. 
The wife called a 2nd time stating that she had been sick and wanted a refund for the entire year since our service was an addon. I explained that they had been informed of this and could have cancelled at any time. 
They received an emailed receipt each month for their payments from My Academy. The wife then stated that she had been sick and that they did not check her emails or credit card statements for several months. They were informed that a letter had been mailed from LHS regarding that our services were an addon to the LHS plan they purchased. LHS decided to move all sales inside and this was the reason our agents were no longer selling the LHS product. A response to the LHS letter was sent out to the membership to remind what services they were getting with an Academy membership. During the 3rd call, I was informed by the husband that they had moved and failed to update their address with Liberty and with My Academy and never received the letters. They also unsubscribed from emails with our system.
The selling agent noted that they had unsubscribed from her emails on 4/5/18.
Both Liberty and My Academy have informed the membership of the change in relationship which only applied to the sales process. Our agents sold the My Academy product with all Liberty Healthshare memberships. The member filled out an online enrollment with My Academy separately from the Liberty Healthshare application. 
Both companies bill separately for the services. This member assumes no consumer responsibility in any way.', 'Jennie Schluth', 'Jennie Schluth', '2019-05-28 12:18:39', '2019-05-28 12:18:39'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000036003009', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000036377153', 'William Moomaw', NULL, '5-28-19 Jennika referred him and he already researched LHS and was concerned about getting hurt on the job from their guideline limitations. He''s healthy. He did have acl surgery March of 2017. He''s not worried about it having problems now. He''s a contractor by trade. Likes PSDHC and PDHC with Redirect. Only about $20 more or less per month. He goes to chiro 1x per week bc feels good for various old injuries. Not sure there''s any medical issue that a chiro would state in records. Lives in Louisville and is 41. Paying $470 to Cigna for bad high ded $6K.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-28 12:18:24', '2019-05-28 12:18:24'),
