  ('zcrm_1579374000035370013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000034162382', 'Juan Rosas', NULL, 'Celeste called in, in regards to her husband Juan, looking to see if a doctor they had recently gone to for a wellness visit was in network. The facility and doctor unfortunately was not in network. She also stated that she was told that they are responsible for paying for a wellness visit. I stopped her there and told her that anything that is preventative, especially an annual wellness visit(as long as it is STRICTLY preventative) is fully covered and what they need to do is present their RCI card to the provider upon arrival. She was very shocked to hear that. She then wanted me to look up providers that are in her area in network. I walked them through how to use the site and they were doing at the same time on their computer. I sent the email that has the instructions how how to properly use the MultiPlan site. She then asked information about 2nd MD and how that works and how to use it. I explained how it works and told her the info on if she goes along the 2nd MD''s suggestions and if she does not go along with their opinion. She was totally understanding of everything I explained, I also sent her the email on how to get in contact with 2nd MD and how it explains everything I had just told her. Lastly I explained to her on what to do if any sort of injury/illness comes up on submitting the bills to Sedera, I sent her the email that explains how to submit the bills. I am also sending her an email on how to present herself to a provider. She was very very happy with the help that I was able to provide to her today and she said she feels much much more comfortable with everything and confident they fully understand how the plan works! -KF', 'Kelly Frederickson', 'Kelly Frederickson', '2019-05-16 10:26:15', '2019-05-16 10:27:19'),
