  ('zcrm_1579374000034909013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011939033', 'Tal Diamant', NULL, 'Tal called in from his doctors office, the staff were saying that they were having a hard time reading his card and he was calling for assistance, I transferred him to Linda over at ASI to speak with him and staff. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-08 16:38:13', '2019-05-08 16:38:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000034909008', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000023796049', 'Andrew Sutton', NULL, 'Andrew and Ashley called in with a barrage of questions wanting to understand how the plan worked.  They said that they should''ve asked them earlier.  Andrew had a question about his Hashimoto''s disease (diagnosed 15 years ago) and wondered what to do with the bills and what happens with the care that he will be receiving yearly.  I first started with Sedera''s 3 year look back of symptoms and diagnosis and went on to tell him that this will not be shared in for year 1, that there will be a cap of 15,000 shared for the next year and 30 for the the 3.  After that it will be shared at 100%.  He asked about naturopathy being sharable, I told him that when he reaches his IUA with it he will have to get preapproval by Sedera first to see if they will share in it. That he would have to ask his doctor to list a treatment plan that show''s that it is curable.  I sent them an email that explains how to open up a need with Sedera.  Next Issue- Ashley took their son for an annual care visit that quickly turned diagnostic because the doctor detected a Murmer.  I had to explain how her sons preventive care visit turned into a diagnostic one, but that she could use the cost of the visit towards their IUA.  I told her that the ultrasound that her son is having tomorrow will go towards that as well.  I told them to call Sedera and let them know what is going on if they think that they will be close or go over their IUA so that Sedera can help guide them through the rest of the process.  Then Ashley had a questions revolving if she were to pregnant or not, I told her that with the amount of specific questions she had that she should really give Sedera a call, I gave her their phone number as well as asked if she would like me to transfer the call to them.  She declined stating that she would call them soon.  There were questions about whether or not medication was covered or not...because Andy has been paying $220 for his thyroid meds.  I sent sent him a prescription quote form to fill out and Kelly Fredrickson found the medication for $10.  She has already sent coupons for him.  This family was very sweet and kept thanking me and pausing to say that they understood more of how the program worked.  ALSO Ashley did not make sure to see if the pediatrician whose name is Pamela Wells was in network or not.  I told her that I would research this on her behalf and get back to her. - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-08 15:37:17', '2019-05-08 15:37:17'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000034909003', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000033451023', 'Scott Ballard', NULL, 'Orlena called in for help concerning filling out her HSA account form.  I texted Patti for some answers and that helped a bit.  I told her our regular business hours and told her that if she had any further questions to to call and ask for Patti Baron.  She was very happy for the support! - KC', 'Kelly Cheever', 'Kelly Cheever', '2019-05-08 15:11:51', '2019-05-08 15:11:51'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000034899023', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000021624001', 'Rachel Holden', NULL, '5-8-19 Rachel and Cami are working together for their non-profit association with the ski and snow sports industry. Mostly 1099 workers who need good options for healthcare. They are ready to present to the Board of Directors. They have all the information already from becoming members themselves. Explained to her they''d have their own click funnel with their logo and such, but I''d do all the work and field the calls. My # will be on the site. We can supply email templates and online flyers if they want, etc. They are excited to share this with their members, assuming the board approves it. Also told them they could waive the $100 fee as added value to members.', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-08 15:05:35', '2019-05-08 15:05:35'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000034899018', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011307064', 'Thomas White-O''Connor', NULL, '5-8-19 "Hi Wendy,

Yes, pretty incredible! You''re welcome for the feedback, I imagine it helps you to know. As for the hospital....it was Boulder Community. They give a 60% discount off the inflated retail prices when you''re self pay - for the hospital portion (which is the big ticket stuff). The individual docs are more like 10-20% for self-pay. I''ve become way too familar with all of this ;-)  Hopefully I''m done with all that for a while. The cardiologist I met with and liked a lot was Dr Nelson Trujillo.

Best
Tom"', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-08 14:47:13', '2019-05-08 14:47:13'),
  ('zcrm_1579374000034899013', 'contact', 'zcrm_1579374000011307064', 'Thomas White-O''Connor', NULL, '5-8-19 "Hi Wendy,

Hope you''re doing well these days. I had another great experience working with Sedera that I thought you''d like to hear about.

I had to have another hospital procedure a few weeks ago. It all turned out well, and I''m fine btw. I had some issues that were raising concerns about my heart, plaque build up, elevated blood pressure, etc. I did a lot of preliminary tests and consults over a long period of time, all of which were inconclusive, met with a Cardiologist and he said the only way to get to the bottom of it was to do a Cardio Catheterization Angiogram. I went ahead and scheduled it right away, since he was about to go out of town. Paid for it upfront, $14,000, trusting/hoping that it would work out with Sedera. I called Sedera to tell them what I was doing, they mentioned that normally in situations like that they recommend the 2nd Opionion, but John Kach was very understanding, and spoke with Sedera about it. I had decided I was going to do it regardless, so I went ahead with it. We negotiated the bill, paid it and sent it to Lauren at Sedera. She was so nice about the whole thing and said she thought they''d be able to work it out, expressed her appreciation with the way we''d negotiated the bill again, etc. About a week later she emails us to say that Sedera was going to cover the cost AND waive our $1000 IUA for the procedure because we''d handled it so well, submitted all the paperwork, negotiated the bill and so on. Beth and I were so amazed and incredulous that an "insurer" could be some human about the whole thing and willing to go beyond what they even needed to do, I''m still amazed and of course Relieved! We haven''t received the payment yet, but I''m confident based on what Lauren said, that it''ll happen.

So, pretty incredible experience and beyond our expectations of what a health care plan could be like, for sure. Thanks again for suggesting Sedera....we really appreciate it!

Best
Tom"', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', 'Wendy Scipione - SR VP National Sales Advisor', '2019-05-08 14:46:49', '2019-05-08 14:46:49'),
